hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22045","(22045) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah al-Ghafiqi and my father. Ta`ma, their master, heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wine has been cursed in ten ways: Cursed is the wine itself, the one who presses it, the one who is pressing it, the one who sells it, the one who buys it, the one who carries it, and the one to whom it is conveyed. And eat its price, and drink it, and drink it. (Abu Dawud 3666. Ahmad 25)"
"22046","(22046) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: I heard him say: It is not permissible to sell wine or drink it."
"22047","(22047) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the selling of alcohol and idols on the Day of Conquest."
"22048","(22048) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Jum, he said: A man asked a donor, he said: I inherited a plant, he said: He sold him grapes, he said: What if I don't find anyone to buy it? He said: So he sold it juice. He said: What if I don’t find anyone to buy it? He said: Do not sell alcohol, for it is not permissible to sell alcohol."
"22049","(22049) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, he said: My father told me, he said: I found ten dinars, so I came to Ibn Abbas and asked him about it, and he said: He identified it on the stone as a Sunnah, but if you do not know it, then give it in charity. Then Its owner came and gave him the choice of reward or fine."
"22050","(22050) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Aamir bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: Abdullah bought a female slave for seven hundred. A dirham, and its owner was absent, so he recited it for a year, or he said: a year, then he went out to the mosque and gave alms and said: Oh God. So yes, but if he refused, then I could do it, then he said: This is what you do to the caught animal, or to the lost animal."
"22051","(22051) Ibn Abi Zayed narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, He said: I heard a man from Muzainah asking the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: What do we find on the crowded path of raindrops? He said: Let her know for a year, and if her companion comes, otherwise, it is yours. (Abu Dawud 1707, Ahmed 180)"
"22052","(22052) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh, who said: Abu Qabil narrated to me, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Amr, that a man said: I picked up a dinar and he said: No one can shelter a stray except a stray. He said: So the man took it in to throw it away. He said: Don't do it. He said: What should I do with it? He said: You will recognize it, and if its companion comes, he will return it to you. Otherwise, give it in charity."
"22053","(22053) Waki’ told us, he said: Mis’ar and Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about He said: Give it to the prince."
"22054","(22054) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Safar, on the authority of a man from Bani Rawas, He said: I picked up three hundred dirhams and gave them a weak definition, and I was in need at that time, so I ate them when I did not find anyone. He recognized her, then she went away and asked Ali, and he said: He recognized her by age, so if her companion comes, give her to him, otherwise give in charity. Otherwise, give him a choice between the reward and a fine for her."
"22055","(22055) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, saying: I heard this hadith from Abu al-Safar, on the authority of A man from Banu Rawas, on the authority of Ali, like him, except he did not say: “Know her.”"
"22056","(22056) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab ordered that the harvest be given its age, and if its owner comes, otherwise he should give it in charity, but if its owner comes, it is better."
"22057","(22057) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Aswad bin Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Nawfal bin Abi Aqrab, on the authority of his father, He said: I picked a full moon and brought it to Omar ibn Al-Khattab, so I said: O Commander of the Faithful, it will save me from it, so he said: And fulfill it. The season, so I brought her to the season, and he said: I introduced her to her, so I introduced her, but I did not find anyone who knew her, so I brought her to him, so I said So he spared her need and said: Shall I not inform you of the best way for her? Give it in charity. If its owner comes and chooses the money, you will be fined for him and the reward will be yours. If he chooses the reward, the reward will be his and you will have whatever. You intend to"
"22058","(22058) Ibn Abi Zay’idah told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’biy, who said: The cut is known as Sunnah, but if you do not find it Ask, then give it to a poor Muslim household, and say to them: This is a loan from its owner to you. If it comes He has more right to it, and if he does not come, then he has more right to it than he did to you."
"22059","(22059) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, he said: It came out Me, Zayd bin Suhhan, and Salman bin Rabi’ah, until we were with Al-Athib and she picked up a whip, and they said to me: Throw it, but I refused. When I came to Medina, I went to Ubayy ibn Ka’b and asked him, and he said: I collected a hundred dinars at the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, and I mentioned that to him, and he said: He recognized it for a year, so if its owner comes, give it to him, otherwise, find out its number. And its vessels and its wards, then you will be like the way of an owner. (Bukhari 2426. Muslim 10)"
"22060","(22060) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who said: I asked Saeed bin al-Musayyab about And he said: He taught it by age and recited its remembrance. If someone comes who knows it, give it to him, otherwise give it in charity. If he comes, give him a choice between the reward and the spectacle."
"22061","(22061) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he said regarding the lump: Recognize it, I do not command you. If you wanted to eat it, you could not take it."
"22062","(22062) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Iyad bin Himar, he said: He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever finds a sting, let a just person, or people of justice, bear witness, and then neither change nor If he comes to his Lord, then he has more right to it. Otherwise, it is God’s wealth. He gives it to whomever He wishes. (Abu Dawud 17061. Ahmad 4/161)"
"22063","(22063) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Abi Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Yazid Mawla Al-Manba’th, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid al-Janni, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the spotting, and he said: Identify it. A year, if its owner comes, otherwise he will spend it. (Bukhari 91. Muslim 1346)"
"22064","(22064) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Faroukh, the client of Umm Salama, who said: A man asked Umm Salama The Prophet’s wife, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: Does the man find a whip? She said: There is no problem with it, the Muslim can use it with his hand. He said: And the shoes? She said: And the shoes? He said: And the containers. She said: I do not permit what God has forbidden. The container is the one that contains the shot."
"22065","(22065) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, found a date and said: Were it not from charity, I would have eaten it."
"22066","(22066) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He found A date and he ate it."
"22067","(22067) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to make a concession from the shots in The belt, the stick, and the whip."
"22068","(22068) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Rabi` ibn Utbah al-Kinani narrated to us, saying: I heard Ata’. He said: There is no harm in He picks up the belt, the stick, and the whip."
"22069","(22069) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qays al-Awdi, on the authority of Bashir: He permitted a shot. About five dirhams."
"22070","(22070) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he is in need of it, let him eat it."
"22071","(22071) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha: She made a concession in the matter of picking up a dirham."
"22072","(22072) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Abu Razin, he said: If you had found it And I need her to eat her."
"22073","(22073) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Maimuna: She found She ate a date and said: God does not like corruption."
"22074","(22074) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of an unnamed sheikh, who said: I saw Ibn Umar finding a date and wiping it, then He gave her a poor person."
"22075","(22075) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Uqba bin Abdullah, he said: Misra bin Umayra narrated to me: He met Abu Hurairah and said: What do you say about the shot? He said: What is the catch? He said: The rope, the reins, and the like. He said: You recognize it, and if you find its companion, you return it to him, otherwise you enjoy it."
"22076","(22076) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: If he is in need of it, he will eat it."
"22077","(22077) Waki’ told us, he said: Salma bin Wardan told us, he said: I asked Salim bin Abdullah about the lost camels? He said: She has her waterskin and her shoes. He left them, unless you know its owner and give them to him. He said: And I asked him about what he lost. The sheep? He said: Identify it. If its owner comes, otherwise it is yours, or your brother’s, or the wolf’s."
"22078","(22078) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather: A man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a lost sheep, and he said: For you, or for your brother, or for a wolf, and he asked him about He strayed from camels and said: What do you want with them? She has her watering can and her shoes, she eats pasture and brings back water."
"22079","(22079) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aliyah, who said: I was sitting with Aisha and she came to her. A woman said: O Mother of the Believers, I found a lost sheep, so what do you command me to do? She said: Know me, milk me, and feed me. Then she asked her again, and Aisha said: You are asking me if I order you to slaughter her. Or sell it, you do not have that right."
"22080","(22080) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhayr bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Salami, and I do not see her except his son Ka’b. She said: I found Finally, on the way to Mecca, I asked Aisha? She said: Enjoy it."
"22081","(22081) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, who said: I was sitting with Abdullah bin Omar when a man came to him and said: Did you find a lost item? He said: Be kind to her and sing. He said: What will happen to me if I drink of her milk? Ibn Omar said: I don’t think you should do that."
"22082","(22082) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The traveler was permitted to carry a whip and a stick. And the sandals."
"22083","(22083) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abdullah bin Badr, on the authority of His father, he said: I found eighty dinars in the reign of Omar bin Al-Khattab, so I brought them to Omar, and he said: He knew them for a year. I said: So if Why didn't you know? He said: Enjoy it."
"22084","(22084) Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Do not raise it from the ground, for you are not of it. Something"
"22085","(22085) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, that Mujahid and Ibn Umar were going around the Kaaba and found Indeed, there are jewels in it, but He did not display any evidence of it."
"22086","(22086) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Surya al-Rabi’ bin Khathim, on the authority of al-Rabi’: He hated taking the shot."
"22087","(22087) Harami bin Amara told us, on the authority of Abu Utba al-Dahhan, who said: I asked Jabir bin Zayd about the fragments they took from The way, his thoughts."
"22088","(22088) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, or Tamim bin Salamah, Mansour doubted, he said Shurayh was passing by with a dinar but it was not presented to him."
"22089","(22089) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Dahhak bin Yasar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: He saw A dinar was thrown out, so he stepped on it with his foot until he brought it close to the place of the Imam, so he left it."
"22090","(22090) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Waqid bin Abdullah narrated to us, saying: I was with Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, and a man asked him: Is it better to leave the shot, or is it better to take it? He said: No, rather they left it."
"22091","(22091) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: I found a piece of grass. He said: Why? Did you take it?"
"22092","(22092) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Al-Furat Al-Makki, who said: I heard a peacock and a man asked him, and he said: I found a dinar. So I took it. He said: Should I put it in its place? He said: I have secured it."
"22093","(22093) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Al-Mundhir bin Jarir, on the authority of his father Jarir, he said: No one takes it, or no one gives it shelter except a lost person. (Abu Dawud 1717. Ahmad 4/362)"
"22094","(22094) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Omar said and he A backrest facing the Kaaba: Whoever takes what is lost is lost."
"22095","(22095) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, he said, `Umar said: No The stray is only a stray.\n Ali said: No one eats a lost animal except a lost person."
"22096","(22096) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Thabit bin Al-Dahhak He said: I found a camel, so I asked Omar, and he said: Identify it, so I identified it, but I did not find anyone who recognized it, so I came to it and said: We have been busy. He said: Send it to where you found it."
"22097","(22097) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli, who said: Whoever takes something seeking the reward, let him not Guarantee on it."
"22098","(22098) Abdul-A’la bin Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a piece of footage is lost, its owner is liable."
"22099","(22099) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ali: Concerning a man who took He lost something, and there was a surplus from him. He said: He is trustworthy."
"22100","(22100) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: Abdullah embraced Islam among his successors, one of whom was Abu Zaydah. Our Lord"
"22101","(22101) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Amer: He did not see any harm in that."
"22102","(22102) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Khusayf, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab: He did not see any harm in that."
"22103","(22103) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: There is no harm in greeting an animal with the owners of the thing if it They are called periods and teeth."
"22104","(22104) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan: He did not see any harm in giving teeth to animals. specified for a specified period."
"22105","(22105) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’: He did not see any harm in greeting animals. And for a man to take without his condition, and with teeth above it, if the soul of the giver and the taker desires that."
"22106","(22106) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran al-Ahwal, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I heard him say: We used to greet the Wasfa’is. Such and such, a span."
"22107","(22107) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muammar bin Sam narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: There is no harm in greeting animals."
"22108","(22108) Rawad bin Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: He did not see anything wrong with greeting the successors if it was A known age."
"22109","(22109) Muhammad bin Maysar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’: He did not see any harm in that."
"22110","(22110) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abu Nazra, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about peace in animals. The successors said: There is no harm in it."
"22111","(22111) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah used to hate peace in the animal."
"22112","(22112) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: that Omar, Hudhayfy, and Ibn Masoud They hated peace in animals."
"22113","(22113) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab: that Zayd bin Khalidah was handed over to Atris bin Arqub in Qalais, so he asked Ibn Masoud? The thought of peace in the animal."
"22114","(22114) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, he said: Omar said: It is usury to pay At the age"
"22115","(22115) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, saying: I witnessed Shariha returning the ladder in the presence of an animal."
"22116","(22116) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, who said: I heard Suwayd bin Ghafali. He hates peace in animals."
"22117","(22117) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Nadr ibn Abi Maryam Abu Laina narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak: He made a concession in peace in The animal, then he turned away from it."
"22118","(22118) Waki’ told us, he said: Hassan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar wrote To Abdullah: Do not greet animals."
"22119","(2219) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of Ammar, the companion of Al-Sabiri, who said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr being asked About peace in animals? So he forbade it and said: You have been in Azerbaijan for a year or two. Do you see them doing it, or do we forbid them? Saeed said: Spread this to someone who does not want it. Hudhayf ibn al-Yaman forbade it."
"22120","(22120) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Abu Nazra, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: Our princes have separated from us. On the authority of him, meaning peace in the animal among the Wasfa’is, he said: So obey your princes if they forbid it, and their princes At that time, the likes of Al-Hakam Al-Ghifari and Abdul-Rahman bin Samurah."
"22121","(22121) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar, who said: Whoever grants a gift will A relative is permissible, and whoever gives a gift to someone other than a relative has more right to it as long as he does not return from it."
"22122","(22122) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Salih, on the authority of Rabi’a ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amir, he said: I was sitting with his father, when two men came to him and were disputing in a flock, and one of them said: I gave him permission. He hoped that he would reward me, and he took my reward and did not reward me, so the other said to him: Give me his reward, I did not ask him, and no I confronted him, and he said: Return his reward to him, or defeat him, for only women and the wickedest of peoples return to talents."
"22123","(22123) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, he said: Omar bin Abdul-Aziz wrote: Whoever grants a gift will not He jumped on her and wanted to return to her, so let him return publicly, not secretly."
"22124","(22124) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn Abza, on the authority of Ali, who said: The man has more right Because of it, what has not been proven from it."
"22125","(22125) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Mujma’, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: A man has more right to be threatened as long as he does not retaliate from her. (Ibn Majah 2387. Daraqutni 180)"
"22126","(22126) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He has more right to her as long as he is not satisfied with her."
"22127","(22127) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Whoever gives in prayer, Or a relative, or a favor, or a right, so your gift is permissible, and the one who asks for forgiveness is rewarded from his gift, or it is returned. Aliyah"
"22128","(22128) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Whoever is rewarded will be rewarded for his face. There is no harm in returning the reward."
"22129","(22129) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Who gave It is for someone other than a relative, so he has the right to take it back unless he approves of it."
"22130","(22130) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, who said: If a man gives the gift, then he has more right to it. As long as it is in his hand, then if he gives it to her, it will be rewarded."
"22131","(22131) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Omar and Ibn Abbas, they said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not permissible for a man to give a gift and then take it back, so his likeness is like that. The dog ate until he was satisfied, vomiting, then he vomited again. (Tirmidhi 1299. Abu Dawud 3533)"
"22132","(22132) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: We have no equal to the evil one. He who returns to his fear is like a dog who returns to his vomit. (Bukhari 2422. Tirmidhi 1298)"
"22133","(22133) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The example of one who returns with his gift is like a dog that eats until it is satisfied and vomits, then returns to vomiting.\n(Ibn Majah 234. Ahmad 2/259)"
"22134","(22134) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: It is not permissible for a man to return to his religion except his father. (Bayhaqi 179. An-Nasa’i 6535)"
"22135","(22135) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The parable of one who returns in his charity is like the parable of a dog who returns in his vomit. (Bukhari 2423. Ahmad 1/54)"
"22136","(22136) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: For example The one who goes back to being frightened, like a dog that vomits and then goes back to vomiting. (Nasa’i 6536)"
"22137","(22137) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The one who returns to his vomit is like the one who returns to his vomit. (Bukhari 2421, Muslim 1241)"
"22138","(22138) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Nothing that a drunk person says is permissible for him.\nAbu Muhammad Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said:"
"22139","(22139) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he said regarding Al-Sakran: As for his sale And buying it is not permissible, and it is in the same position as a fool."
"22140","(22140) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He did not permit its sale or purchase."
"22141","(22141) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he said, “In a garment between two legs, half of it is on One of them for ten, and his half to the other for ten. They said: If he sells it bargained, or on a profitable basis, then it is two halves. Between them."
"22142","(22142) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Al-Hakam: Concerning two men who bought goods. One of them sold half of it for twenty, and the other bought half of it for ten, and Al-Sha’bi said: If he sold it for a profit, then he would pay his principal. Their money, and if he sold it by bargaining, then half and half, and the arbitrator said: It is between them two halves."
"22143","(22143) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ziyad Al-Alam, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If he sold it for a profit The profit is on the capital, and if he sells it bargaining, then it is between them, and the same applies to his commanders."
"22144","(22144) Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir ibn Hazim, who said: Hammad was asked about goods between two men being carried out. One of them is worth more than what the other is worth. He said: The profit is according to the amount of their capital."
"22145","(22145) Hafs told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He was asked about the man The mortgager takes a pawn and says: If I do not bring it to you such-and-such, is it yours? He said: He does not have that."
"22146","(22146) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who makes a mortgage with him, and the man who pledges it says: If I do not give you With it to such-and-such, then it is yours. He said: The mortgage will not be closed, even if he said: If I do not bring it to you to such-and-such. So sell him and take back what you have. He said: He is not trustworthy himself, nor will he sell him."
"22147","(22147) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas, on the authority of Bashir bin A prohibition, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever frees a person belonging to him among his slaves, or A share, so his salvation is in his wealth if he has wealth, but if he does not have wealth, the servant must ask for its value. He is not to be blamed for it.\n(Bukhari 2492, Muslim 1140)"
"22148","(22148) Abu Asama and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If he is solvent, he is liable, and if he is insolvent, then what he has freed will be freed. (Muslim 1139. Abu Dawud 3939)"
"22149","(22149) Ibn Numair told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever frees a young man He has a slave. He guarantees his wealth to his companions if he has any, and Ibn Umar said: If he does not have any money, the slave will strive."
"22150","(22150) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, he said: It was among me. And between the lions and our mother there was a boy who had witnessed al-Qadisiyah and performed well in it, so they wanted to free him, and I was young, so he mentioned That black one belonged to Omar, and Omar said: Free yourself, and Abd al-Rahman will be in charge of him until he desires as you desire. In it, or he takes his share."
"22151","(22151) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, who said: He was a boy Between me and my brothers, I wanted to free him, so I went to Ibn Masoud and mentioned that to him, and he said: Do not spoil your partners. So they were safe, but wait until they grow old."
"22152","(22152) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar, the same."
"22153","(22153) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: There were thirty Among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, they guarantee a man’s freedom of a slave between him and his owner, if he is well-off."
"22154","(22154) Azhar al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad: That a slave was between two men, and one of them freed him. So he rode his partner to Omar, and he was destined to establish the highest status over him."
"22155","(22155) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Shu’bi, he said: If there was a Sharih, he would have imprisoned him for it."
"22156","(22156) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning the servant being between two men. So he frees one of them from his share. He said: He is guaranteed if he has money, but if he does not have money, the servant must seek help."
"22157","(22157) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asama bin Zaid, he said: I asked Suleiman bin Yassar about him, and he said: Like that, I said to him: He is young? He said: The Sunnah."
"22158","(22158) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: If a man frees a share of a slave There is a share in it, so he guarantees what is left of it if he is well off, and if he is in difficulty, the servant should seek help."
"22159","(22159) Muhammad bin Musar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father: Concerning a servant who is between two So one of them freed his share, and he said: He is a guarantor for the share of its owner."
"22160","(22160) Yahya bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir: Concerning a slave who was between two men and was freed. One of them is his share. He said: He will complete his emancipation. If he does not have any money, the slave may ask for half, and the loyalty will be For the one who freed"
"22161","(22161) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ismail bin Raji, on the authority of Abu Majliz: That a slave was between two men, and one of them freed his share. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, imprisoned him until he sold it. Therein are spoils for him. (Musnad 1513)"
"22162","(22162) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhayr, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim and Ash-Shu’abi: In the servant there is between the two men, and one of them frees his share. They said: It is freed from the property of the one who freed it and guarantees its owner for its value. Justice on the day I free him."
"22163","(22163) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Justice among Muslims is he who has not been impugned. Abdomen, not vulva."
"22164","(22164) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Amer, who said: It is permissible for a Muslim man to bear witness unless he He will suffer a punishment, or he will become aware of something bad in his religion."
"22165","(22165) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to accept the testimony of those who prayed, except that The opponent does what will hurt him."
"22166","(22166) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Habib, who said: Umar asked a man, about a man, and he said: We know nothing but good, so he said: Umar. : Enough for you"
"22167","(22167) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Shurayh said: Invite and multiply and recite and come. On this with just witnesses, for we have been commanded to do justice, and you are far from it. So if they say: God knows best, then God knows best. They differ in that they say: He is suspicious, and a suspicious witness is not permissible. If they say: We have taught him to be just, a Muslim is just. God willing, likewise, and your testimony is permissible."
"22168","(22168) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: I bought a female slave and her family stipulated that I should not sell. I neither fear nor command, so if you die, will you be free? So I asked Al-Hakam bin Utaiba? He said: There is no harm in it.\n And you asked an alcoholic? He said: There is no problem with it. I said: Are you afraid of him? He said: Yes, I hope you will be rewarded for it.\n Did you ask someone to give, or was he asked? His thoughts\n Al-Awza’i said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The sale is permissible and the condition is invalid. And I asked Abdah bin Abi Lubabah? He said: This is bad relief.\n I asked Al-Zuhri and he told me: Ibn Masoud wrote to Omar asking him about a female slave he had bought from his wife. If he sells it, he has more right to the price. Omar said: Do not step on an open space that has anyone else in it."
"22169","(22169) Waki’ and Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Omar said: It is not of your wealth whatever it was. Therein is a Mathnawiyah for others."
"22170","(22170) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha: She hated it. That the slave girl be sold on the condition that she is not sold."
"22171","(22171) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Khusayf, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr; Concerning a man who buys a slave girl on the condition that he will not sell it or give it away. He said: He will not be close to her."
"22172","(22172) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father: He hated her."
"22173","(22173) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He used to say: Do not have intercourse with private parts. There is a condition in it."
"22174","(22174) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who buys a female slave for That he does not sell it or give it away. He said: It is nothing."
"22175","(22175) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: Concerning a man who buys a slave girl. Provided that he will not sell it, give it away, or give it away. He said: I wish I had found it and bought it under this condition, and I stipulate For them, she is freed when she dies."
"22176","(22176) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he said: Every condition in a sale It is nullified by the sale except emancipation, and every condition in marriage is nullified by the marriage except divorce."
"22177","(22177) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A woman came and said: My daughter It was bought on the condition that it would not be sold. He said: Your daughter is on her terms."
"22178","(22178) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Burqan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba: Ibn Masoud bought a maid from his daughter Zainab and stipulated: If he sells her, he has more right to her for the price. So Ibn Masoud asked Masoud Omar decided to have intercourse with her."
"22179","(22179) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Imran bin Umair: That Omar said to Abdullah: Do not approach her."
"22180","(22180) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Badr, on the authority of Abu Yahya Al-Araj, he said: The Prophet was asked May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of a servant who was freed by his master upon his death, and he had no other wealth and was in debt. He said: So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to strive in religion. (Abdul Razzaq 16766)"
"22181","(22181) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Ali was asked about a man who freed a slave of his at When he died and he had no other wealth, and he owed a debt, he said: He will be freed and he will strive for value."
"22182","(22182) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: A woman emancipated a female slave of hers, and she had no other property. Abdullah said: You strive for its value."
"22183","(22183) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who freed a slave of his. He fell ill, then he died with a debt on him and no other wealth. He said, “He will strive for its value, if the value is greater.” Of the religion, he strives for the creditors in their religion, and considering what is left, two-thirds belong to the heirs and he has one-third."
"22184","(22184) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: Concerning a man who freed his slave when he died and had no wealth. Others, he said: He evaluates what is just, then strives for its value."
"22185","(22185) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, that he was asked about a man He freed a servant of his during his illness and he had no other property. He said: I will repay him in its entirety for something that he made for God, but I will not return it.\n Shurayh said: I allow one-third of it and I seek refuge in two-thirds of it."
"22186","(22186) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: I said to Al-Sha’bi: Which of the two sayings do you most admire? He said: The saying of Masruq is more interesting to me in giving a fatwa, and the saying of Shurayh is more beloved to me in giving a ruling."
"22187","(22187) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: He shall be freed. a third"
"22188","(22188) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, who said: Abraham said about a man who freed a servant of his at His death and he had no other wealth, so Abraham said: He frees one-third of him and works for two-thirds of him."
"22189","(22189) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a man recommends that a slave of his be emancipated, So it is from a third, and if it is more than a third, he can work with what he exceeds."
"22190","(22190) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: They claimed that Al-Hasan was saying about a man who freed some of his kings when His death, he said: He will free what he has freed and he will be rewarded with what remains."
"22191","(22191) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning a man who freed a third of his slave during his illness, he said: It is held in a third of it, and if he gave commandments, the servant will seek help."
"22192","(22192) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he freed some of his slaves When he fell ill, he freed all of it, but if it was more than a third, then he ran with what was left of the third."
"22193","(22193) Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Hisham was asked about a man who freed a slave from one of his slaves upon his death, so he told us about Hafs bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: It is in a third of it, no more than that."
"22194","(22194) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi. On the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: The testimony of hearing is permissible."
"22195","(22195) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man heard something from a people, it would be The judge comes and says: They did not call me to witness, but I heard such-and-such and such-and-such."
"22196","(22196) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Furat, on the authority of his father Furat, who said: I owed a man fifty dirhams. So I went to sue him while a man was listening, so I took him to Shurayh, and he denied me. Shurayh said: I explained to you, so I said: A man who was He heard and he acknowledged me, so he said: Call upon him, so I called upon him and he testified, so he said: Get up and I will give him his due."
"22197","(22197) Ubaidah bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Kulthum bin Al-Aqmar, he said: Shuraih did not A hidden witness is permitted."
"22198","(22198) Ubaidah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr’s statement, he said: Al-Sha’bi would not allow a hidden witness to be a witness."
"22199","(22199) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not permissible to be a witness who is hidden."
"22200","(22200) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, that he did not permit a witness. The one who hides, he said: Amr bin Harith said: This is what is done to the unjust traitor, or the immoral person said."
"22201","(22201) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim and Ash-Shu’bi, who said: When the polytheists come to you and judge you concerning between them according to the rule of Muslims, so do not repeat it to anyone else, or turn away from them, and leave them and their people of religion."
"22202","(22202) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: I asked about the Jewish government. And the Christians, when they refer to us? He said: Judge between them according to your ruling regarding the Muslims. Nothing is permissible between them except what is permissible between the Muslims."
"22203","(22203) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Be alone with the people of The Book and its laws, so when they rise to you, establish over them what is in your Book."
"22204","(22204) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Qaboos bin Mukhariq, on the authority of his father, he said: He sent Ali Muhammad bin Abi Bakr was the prince of Egypt, so Muhammad wrote to Ali asking him about a Muslim who committed suicide as a Christian? Then Ali wrote: “Implement the punishment on the Muslim who committed adultery with Christianity, and raise the case of Christianity to the Christians who will be judged.” In it whatever they want."
"22205","(22205) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: These verses have been abrogated {And that I judge between them according to what God has revealed} {Judge between them, or turn away from them}"
"22206","(22206) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he wishes, he may rule, and if he wishes, he may not. He rules."
"22207","(22207) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stoned a Jew. There are Jews with a Jew and a hypocrite. (Abu Dawud 4449)"
"22208","(22208) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samarra: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stoned a Jew. And a Jew\n(Tirmidhi 1437. Ahmad 5/91)"
"22209","(22209) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, and Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra: on the authority of Al-Bara’, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, stoned a Jew. (Muslim 1327. Abu Dawud 4444)"
"22210","(22210) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was stoned. Jewish and Jewish. (Muslim 1328. Abu Dawud 4448)"
"22211","(22211) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He stoned two Jews. I am among those who stoned them. (Muslim 1326. Abu Dawud 4443)"
"22212","(22212) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Kurdous, on the authority of his father: that a man was punished in He testified about the wine, and he asked me about it. So I said: He is one of the best of our youth, so he accepted your testimony."
"22213","(22213) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Umar: Omar wrote to Abu Musa about a man who drank alcohol: If he repents, then accept his testimony."
"22214","(22214) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Izza, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: He permitted the witness of a man. He was dipped in wine."
"22215","(22215) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Musa, on the authority of Omar ibn Abdul Aziz: He permitted A brother’s testimony to his brother."
"22216","(22216) Ibn Fadil narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, who said: Two men from the neighborhood had rivalries, and one of them, his brother from his father and mother, testified with Shurayh, and the man said: You are his brother, so he said: So... Who do you testify against? He said: No. He said to his opponent: How can I refute your testimony?"
"22217","(22217) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The least permissible is the testimony of a brother to his brother."
"22218","(22218) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is permissible for a brother to bear witness to his brother."
"22219","(22219) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Othman Al-Bati, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: with the same."
"22220","(22220) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muzahim bin Abi Muzahim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Al-Zubayr: He permitted the testimony of a brother to his brother."
"22221","(22221) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is permissible for a brother to bear witness to his brother."
"22222","(22222) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: It is permissible for a brother to bear witness to his brother if He was just."
"22223","(22223) Ubaidah bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Harb bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Shurayh: He granted the testimony of a brother to his brother."
"22224","(22224) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Harith, who said: A man ate on the right side of Shurayh, and Shurayh made up his mind. The man said: I swear, and Shurayh said: My judgment has passed."
"22225","(22225) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: He commanded him to He asked a woman to take an oath, but she refused to do so, so he forced her to do so."
"22226","(22226) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Salem: That Ibn Umar sold a boy of his for eight hundred dirhams, and the buyer found a defect in it, so he disputed it with Othman, and Othman said to him: Othman: I sold it for the money, but he refused. He swore, but Othman rejected him."
"22227","(22227) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah and Ibn Shubarmah, who said: Abdullah bought a boy for Imru’, so when he took him to His house: The boy’s fever came, so he came to return the boy, so he disputed with him to Al-Sha’abi and said to Abdullah: Did you know that he spoiled you with a defect? He said: I have no proof. So he said to the man: Swear that you did not sell him to a slave. The man said: I will return the oath to Abdul. By God, Al-Sha’bi decided to take the oath upon him, and said: Either you swear, or else the boy will punish you."
"22228","(22228) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit used to take a reward as a judge."
"22229","(22229) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Masruq: He was not taken to court. reward\n He mentioned something similar on the authority of Al-Qasim, or something like this."
"22230","(22230) Muhammad ibn Marwan al-Basri narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus ibn Abi al-Furat, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: He hated that Ali be seized. Judgment is rewarded."
"22231","(22231) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Husayn, on the authority of al-Qasim, on the authority of Omar, who said: It is not appropriate for a judge to The Muslims are not to take a reward, nor is the owner of their spoils."
"22232","(22232) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad: He did not see any harm in taking the judge Sustenance from the treasury of Muslims."
"22233","(22233) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, he said: We have been informed, or he said: It has informed me that Ali was blessed with five hundred companions."
"22234","(22234) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He used to forbid selling The fruit until it is nourished, and Ibn Omar said: until its goodness appears."
"22235","(22235) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Wakee’, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Omar said: It is usury to be sold. The fruit was not ripe."
"22236","(22236) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: Do not greet a palm tree until it turns yellow, or It turns red, and there is no seed in it when it is green until it has ears."
"22237","(22237) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He forbade selling the fruit until it appears to be good. (Bukhari 2183, Muslim 1167)"
"22238","(22238) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The palm tree will not be sold until its kernels are strong and secure. Blessing be upon him."
"22239","(22239) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Kharijiyah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit: He used to sell Its fruit when the Pleiades comes out."
"22240","(22240) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’ and Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet forbade praying. May God bless him and grant him peace from selling fruits until their goodness appears. (Muslim 861, Ahmad 3/381)"
"22241","(22241) Yahya bin Sa’id al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Kathir, who said: I heard Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab says: The fruit is not sold until it is ripe and is safe from harm."
"22242","(22242) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade selling The fruit until it appears to be good. It was said to Anas: What does it seem to be good? He said: It turns red or turns yellow. (Bukhari 2198, Muslim 1190)"
"22243","(22243) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Bukair bin Amir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Palm trees are not sold until they turn red or turn yellow."
"22244","(22244) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If some of it turns red, there is no problem. With your purchase"
"22245","(22245) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Umm Thawr, on the authority of her husband Bishr, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: When are palm trees sold? He said: If it turns red or yellow."
"22246","(22246) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Zayd ibn Thabit said: Do not buy the fruit until it ripens. The Pleiades\n Al-Zuhri said: I mentioned that to Salim bin Abdullah, and he said: The curse will come after the Pleiades have risen.\n(Abdul Razzaq 14316)"
"22247","(22247) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, who said: A man asked Ibn Umar about buying fruit? He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade that the fruit be sold until its goodness appears."
"22248","(22248) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Omar and Abdullah, that they said: No. Palm trees are sold until they turn red or turn yellow."
"22249","(22249) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote that the fruit should not be sold. Until her goodness appears."
"22250","(22250) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yazid ibn Khumayr, on the authority of a servant of Quraysh, who said: I heard Abu Huraira narrated to Muawiyah, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade selling fruits until they are harvested from all of them. Accidental\n(Abu Dawud 3362. Ahmad 2/387)"
"22251","(22251) Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, he said: Al-Qasim and Makhul narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imamah, he said : The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling the fruit until its goodness appears. (Tabarani 7592)"
"22252","(22252) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Do not buy the fruit until it appears to be good. They said: What does it appear to be good? He said: Until her illness goes away and her perfume ends."
"22253","(22253) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Fudayl bin Ghazwan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abi Huraira: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling the fruit until it appears to be good. (Muslim 561 Ahmad 2/262)"
"22254","(22254) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The master takes from the wealth of someone he owns. Whatever he wants"
"22255","(22255) Azhar Al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad was asked about a man who took from his servant’s wealth? He said: I do not know that this is part of ihsan."
"22256","(22256) Shababi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij Jabir bin Abdullah and Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: Whoever has a male slave who goes out and a female slave whom he goes around does not have a slave. To take something from what He gave them."
"22257","(22257) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: Umar bin Abdul-Aziz wrote: That a judge should not sit in court. If the polytheists enter the mosque, then they are unclean. God Almighty said: {The polytheists are only unclean}."
"22258","(22258) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna bin Saeed, who said: I saw Al-Hasan and Zurara bin Awfa making two decisions in Al-Rahba coming out of the mosque."
"22259","(22259) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman bin Qays narrated to us, he said: I saw Yahya bin Omar judge in The mosque"
"22260","(22260) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Ja`d ibn Dhakwan, on the authority of Shuraih: That it was when the day A bird who ruled in his home."
"22261","(22261) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ghani, who said: I saw Al-Hasan performing the prayer in the mosque."
"22262","(22262) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri and his followers, who said: The People of the Book, the slave, and the child when They had a witness, so the People of the Book converted to Islam, the servant was freed, and the child grew up, so their testimony is permissible, except that It will be rejected and so will they."
"22263","(22263) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: Concerning a servant who gives testimony, and it is rejected, then He emancipates, he said: It is not permissible."
"22264","(22264) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to say regarding the slave and the non-Muslim, when they testify, it is rejected. Their testimony, then he freed this one, or converted this one to Islam: Their testimony is permissible."
"22265","(22265) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If a servant testifies, his testimony is rejected. Then he was freed. He said: It is not permissible, and the arbiter said: It is permissible."
"22266","(22266) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awanan, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of his father, he said: If he testifies The slave had his testimony rejected, then he was freed, for it is not permissible."
"22267","(22267) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Shurayh, that he said: If the servant bears witness His testimony was rejected, then he was freed. He said: It is not permissible."
"22268","(22268) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib and Ata: Omar ibn al-Khattab said regarding the Jew, the Christian, and the slave: If they testify to a witness, they will not confirm it until the Jew and the Christian are freed and delivered, Their testimony is permissible."
"22269","(22269) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Ibn Suraqi narrated to me: that Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah wrote To the people of Deir Taya: I have guaranteed you that your blood, your property, and your churches will not be destroyed or destroyed unless you speak out. Or give shelter to a new innovator, for if you have done so, or have given shelter to a new innovator, then you are cleared of responsibility. It is your duty to lodge the guest for three days, and we are free from the obligation of the army. Khalid bin Al-Walid, Yazid bin Abi Sufyan, Shurahbil bin Hassani, and Quda’i bin Amir all witnessed and wrote. (Saeed bin Mansour 2605)"
"22270","(22270) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, who said: Omar ibn al-Khattab passed by a scribe writing among the people. And he testified more than two times, so he forbade him, then he passed by and said: Did I not forbid you? The man said: I obeyed God and disobeyed you.\n And about the truthfulness of Omar: Abdullah bin Al-Arqam and Mu’aqib witnessed. And so-and-so and so-and-so witnessed and wrote about Ali’s truthfulness."
"22271","(22271) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Jarrah, he said: Musa bin Salem told me, he said: When Al-Hajjaj evacuated his family A woman came to me with a letter claiming that the one who emancipated her father said: This is what Talha bin Ubaidullah bought from so-and-so, son of so-and-so. He bought from him his girl a dinar or a dirham for five hundred dirhams, good, good, and beautiful, and he paid the price to him. And he freed him for the sake of God, for no one has a way against him except the path of loyalty. Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam and Abdullah bin Amer and Ziad."
"22272","(22272) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, who said: If a man buys his slave girl and she has a defect and it happens There is another flaw in it. He said: The last nullifies the first."
"22273","(22273) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, that he used to say: If he had an illness other than that Pet him for him, and he will go with him and give him as much of his price as that one who is in need of him."
"22274","(22274) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It used to be said: Return the pest with its beginning. If a defect occurs, it is the buyer’s property, and the seller will return the value of the defect."
"22275","(22275) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: It is from the buyer’s money, and it can be returned. The seller's defect value."
"22276","(22276) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, who said: A man passed by a people among whom was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He had a garment. I saw him saying: A garment. Some of them said to him: How much did you buy? I see him saying: It is more than its price, then he said: I lied, and among them was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he returned. He said: O Messenger of God, you bought it for such-and-such without what it was, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Give in charity. Thanks (Abu Dawud 164)"
"22277","(22277) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He disliked peace in the meat."
"22278","(22278) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in greeting people with peace if they see it at a certain extent."
"22279","(22279) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Amr, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Tawoos: He hated fresh meat. Women"
"22280","(22280) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’: He did not see. It is difficult to make peace with meat if it has a known limit."
"22281","(22281) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos: He disliked wearing silk, thin sabers, and commercial goods. What is it?"
"22282","(22282) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, who said: I heard Azhar ask Ata’ about selling Al-Riqaq wine. He thought about it."
"22283","(22283) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Ata’ said: Silk is more beloved to me than saber."
"22284","(22284) Abd al-Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abd al-Rahman al-Dalani, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Sayegh, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar: Concerning a slave between two, and one of them freed his share. He said: He must free the rest of him, but if not Then the slave ran for his neck, and they were partners in loyalty."
"22285","(22285) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he is solvent, he is liable, and loyalty is to him, even if he is insolvent. The servant strove, and loyalty was between them."
"22286","(22286) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir, who said: The servant strives and loyalty is to the one who emancipate"
"22287","(22287) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad: Concerning a servant who was between two men and one of them freed him. He said: Loyalty between them means if the servant seeks help."
"22288","(22288) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Loyalty is to the one who is freed. Whether the servant strives, or does he not strive."
"22289","(22289) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: Habib, who used to stand at the head of Shurayh, told me : He imprisoned his son Abdullah as a guarantee for a man who guaranteed him himself."
"22290","(22290) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: If the boy is in the tax office, he buys something for sale. On her neck.\n Hammad said: If his master gives permission to sell; In his neck."
"22291","(22291) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith and Hammad: If a man boycotts his slaves over taxes, then he He gave him permission"
"22292","(22292) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The one who manages One-third"
"22293","(22293) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: The one who manages from a third."
"22294","(22294) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi: that Ali used to make the one who managed it from a third, and that Amir He used to make it from a third."
"22295","(22295) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: It is from a third, and Masruq said: He is empty of all money."
"22296","(22296) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, Al-Amash and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The one who manages from the third."
"22297","(22297) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalaba: that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: The one who manages is from the third. (Abdul Razzaq 16657)"
"22298","(22298) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: The one who manages from a third."
"22299","(22299) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: The one who manages is from a third."
"22300","(22300) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Rabi`, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: He is from all Money"
"22301","(22301) Shababi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The one who manages all the wealth."
"22302","(22302) Shadhan narrated to us, he said: Yahya bin Hamza narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ and Al-Nu’man, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: The one who manages One-third"
"22303","(22303) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir, who said: The one who manages is from the third."
"22304","(22304) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: In the shroud It is from the capital of the total capital, not from the third."
"22305","(22305) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The shroud is from all the wealth."
"22306","(22306) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If the money is a lot, then from all the money, and if It was little, it was a third."
"22307","(22307) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: The shroud is from all wealth."
"22308","(22308) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The shroud is from all wealth."
"22309","(22309) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The shroud is from the capital of the total capital, not from A third, and nothing else."
"22310","(22310) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab and al-Hasan, who said: The shroud is from all Money"
"22311","(22311) Waki` told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Khalas, who said: The shroud is made of one-third.\n Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: From all the money."
"22312","(22312) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of the ruling, he said: The shroud is from all the wealth."
"22313","(22313) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Jahm, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: From all the wealth."
"22314","(22314) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The shroud is from all the wealth."
"22315","(22315) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, he said: The shroud is from all Money"
"22316","(22316) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amir, who said: The woman is shrouded from her share."
"22317","(22317) His youth narrated to us, he said: His people narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, he said: The shroud is made of all wealth."
"22318","(22318) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Mu’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The shroud is from all the wealth."
"22319","(22319) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, who said: You will be shrouded from a third."
"22320","(22320) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair Al-Absi: That a man picked up a foundling and brought him to Ali. So he freed him."
"22321","(22321) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, some years ago he heard Abu Jamil say: I found an outcast, so he mentioned him. Arifi to Omar, so I went to him and he said: He is free, and his loyalty is yours and his breastfeeding is upon us. (Imam Malik 19)"
"22322","(22322) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning the foundling, he said: His intention is if he intends to If he is free, then he is free, and if he intends to be a slave, then he is a slave."
"22323","(22323) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The foundling is free."
"22324","(22324) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Amer, he said: The foundling is free."
"22325","(22325) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: A bastard cannot be kept as a slave."
"22326","(22326) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The foundling is free."
"22327","(22327) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of a man from the Ansar: Omar bin Al-Khattab freed a bastard."
"22328","(22328) Waki’ told us, he said: Shuabi told us, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about the foundling? They said: He is free.\n Shu`ba said: So I said to the arbitrator: From whom? He said: On the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Basri, on the authority of Ali."
"22329","(22329) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhayr bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Dhul bin Aws, on the authority of Tamim bin Masih said: I left the house and had no child, and I found a foundling, so I brought him to Ali and he dipped him into his water. (Abdul Razzaq 13841)"
"22330","(22330) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hout, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He said: Omar: They are owned."
"22331","(22331) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Musa al-Jinni, he said: I saw a child born of adultery and he was inflicted on him in His water"
"22332","(22332) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habib bin Abi Thabit, who said: The letter of Omar bin Abd came. Dear to the people of Mecca, the foundling is free."
"22333","(22333) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: He hated to be described as a The man with the commodity does not have it."
"22334","(22334) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He hated the specifications."
"22335","(22335) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad: He hated it."
"22336","(22336) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: The man says : Buy this sale and I will buy it from you as you like it."
"22337","(22337) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Abi Al-Fadl, he said: I heard Al-Hasan and he asked him about a man bargaining with another man for freedom. So he says: I don't have it, so he says: Buy it so I can buy it from you? He thought about it and said: These are the specifications."
"22338","(22338) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad: He did not see any harm in it."
"22339","(22339) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, he said: I said to Tawus: The man He bargains with me for the goods and I do not have them, so he says: Buy and I will buy from you, and if it were not for his position I would not have bought it? His idea is peacock."
"22340","(22340) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man saying to another man: Buy this garment. I will buy it from you as you like it."
"22341","(22341) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Do not buy wool on its apparent appearance. Sheep, nor milk from udders."
"22342","(22342) Mulazim bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zufar bin Zayd, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Abu Hurairah about buying milk. In the udders? He forbade me from him."
"22343","(22343) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Jadham bin Abdullah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, On the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade buying what is in the stomachs of livestock. Until she gives birth, and there is nothing in her udders except as a measure."
"22344","(22344) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father: He disliked selling milk from udders except How much?"
"22345","(22345) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He hated selling milk in the udders of a sheep."
"22346","(22346) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Wahhab bin Uqba, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about a people who used to buy cow’s milk. A certain number of days, then they will buy it? He said: It will not work except hand in hand."
"22347","(22347) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Omar ibn Farrukh al-Qattab narrated to us, he heard it from Habib ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling milk in a udder, or ghee in milk. (Abu Dawud 1831, Darqutni 45)"
"22348","(22348) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He disliked buying milk from the udder of a sheep."
"22349","(22349) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Tawus And Mujahid: They both disliked selling milk from udders."
"22350","(22350) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: In Paradise there is a palace called Eden, surrounded by towers and meadows, and five thousand gates. No one can live in it, or no one can enter it except A prophet, a truthful person, a martyr, or a just imam."
"22351","(22351) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ammar said: There are three who do not disdain their rights except An obvious hypocrite: a just imam, a teacher of goodness, and one who has gray hair in Islam. (Tabarani 7819)"
"22352","(22352) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, who said: The work of a just imam is better than One of you worked for sixty years."
"22353","(22353) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Mikhraq, on the authority of Abu Kinana, on the authority of Abu Musa, He said: Among the honor of God is honoring the gray-haired Muslim, and the bearer of the Qur’an, neither exaggerating in it nor neglecting it, and honoring Possessor of just authority."
"22354","(22354) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sa’dan al-Janni narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’d Abi Mujahid al-Tai’i, on the authority of Abi Mudalliyah, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The just Imam will not have his supplication rejected.\n(Ibn Majah 1752. Ahmad 2/304)"
"22355","(22355) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Abraham: Concerning a people who wanted to dig in Their house or bathroom. He said: It is their property and they can do with it whatever they want."
"22356","(22356) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zayd told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Ash’u: He blocked a well. His neighbor dug it behind his wall."
"22357","(22357) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan: In a wall in a people’s house, he said: If he wants, he can dig into it. Dad"
"22358","(22358) Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: : Do not struggle in the pits. (Abu Dawud 408, Bayhaqi 156)"
"22359","(22359) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr: That a man said to his servant: Stay with so-and-so, but if you separate from him, you are free. So he said: They bear witness that I have emancipated him. This was brought to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, the Emir of Mecca, and he approved his emancipation. He said: So it was. Al-Hassan sees that."
"22360","(22360) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: I was informed that Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: No. He is freed."
"22361","(22361) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr bin Ibrahim Al-Ansari, on the authority of his uncle Al-Dahhak, who said: Two men disputed with Omar ibn al-Khattab and claimed his testimony. Omar said to them: If you wish, I will testify, but I will not judge between you. I decided whatever you wanted and I did not bear witness."
"22362","(22362) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, who said: A woman came to Shurayh and came to him. With a witness. He said: Bring me another witness. She said: You are a witness. So he made her take an oath and decided for her."
"22363","(22363) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I do not agree to be a judge or witness."
"22364","(22364) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, he said: I asked him about a man who had money over another man. So he had two witnesses testify against him, and one of the witnesses asked for justice? Al-Sha’bi said: A man came to Shurayh and argued with him, and I was sitting with him. Then the other man came with a witness against him, then he said to Shurayh: You You bear witness for me, so Shurayh said: Come to the prince so that I may bear witness for you. (Bayhaqi 10)"
"22365","(22365) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’: He used to hate goldsmiths’ dust, meaning: buying it."
"22366","(22366) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He used to hate buying goldsmiths’ dust unless he bought it. Gold dust with silver and silver dust with gold."
"22367","(22367) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Al-Ja’d, who said: I asked Al-Sha’abi about buying goldsmiths’ dust? He thought about it and said: It is deception.\n Muhammad said: My father used to buy it with offers."
"22368","(22368) Harami bin Amara told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in buying dirt. Gold for silver and silver dust for gold."
"22369","(22369) Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Burdan bin Abi Al-Nadr, who said: I was selling food to a man, and he gave the man What is the fee for a measurer? So I asked Al-Sha’abi about that? He said: Give it to him, for it is only upon you."
"22370","(22370) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, or Ibn Abi Maliki and Amr ibn Dinar, who said: We are still We hear that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decreed that a dinar or ten dirhams be given to the absent slave who was found leaving the Sacred Mosque."
"22371","(22371) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Amr al-Shaybani: That a man struck A slave was missing a large amount of dates, so he brought it, and Ibn Masoud put forty dirhams in it."
"22372","(22372) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: That Omar was placed in Make the abaq a dinar, or twelve dirhams."
"22373","(22373) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, Like him"
"22374","(22374) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Abi Maliki informed me: that Omar bin Abd Al-Aziz ruled that the abrogator be given three dinars if he was taken on his journey."
"22375","(22375) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of his leaders and Abi Hashim: that Umar decided to make The last one is forty dirhams."
"22376","(22376) Yahya bin Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jurays, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: No. It's okay to make a fugitive."
"22377","(22377) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The Muslim responds to The Muslim"
"22378","(22378) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I was given the Ja’al in the time of Muawiyah forty A dirham."
"22379","(22379) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh. On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Shuraih, that he used to say: If it is taken in Egypt, then ten dirhams. If it is taken from Egypt, it is forty dirhams."
"22380","(22380) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hakam: He said regarding the previous one: It is taken. He said: The Muslim responds to The Muslim"
"22381","(22381) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika and Amr bin Dinar, who said: The Prophet made May God bless him and grant him peace, a dinar is given to the absent slave when he is brought out of the Sacred Mosque."
"22382","(22382) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, he said: I said to Abdullah bin Utbah: Do you make a mistake? The one who stays? He said: Yes, I said: Al-Hurr? He said: No."
"22383","(22383) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, he said: If He did not give him a reward, let him send him to the place he took him."
"22384","(22384) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Masruq, who said: If the judge takes Hadiyyah, he has committed illicit things, and if he takes a bribe, it amounts to disbelief."
"22385","(22385) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muadh bin Al-Ala’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: Ali delivered a speech in Kufa. And in his hand was a flask, and he said: I have never seen anything with it since I entered it except this. He gave it to me as a gift."
"22386","(22386) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Al-Muhajir, who said: Al-Asabdhu was given to Abdul-Hamid. Forty thousand, or less, or more, so he wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he wrote to him: If he would give a gift. If you are on the island, accept it from him. Otherwise, count it as his tax."
"22387","(22387) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It used to be said: Bribery in government is unlawful."
"22388","(22388) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, he said: Omar said: There are two chapters of unlawful acts that people eat: bribes. And the dowry of the adulteress."
"22389","(22389) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Murah, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr, About the illicit? He said: bribery."
"22390","(22390) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Qaz’a, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The gifts of princes are deceptions."
"22391","(22391) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Qaz’a, on the authority of Abu Yazid al-Madani, who said: Jabir bin Abdullah was asked about Gifts for princes? He said: There is a deception in my soul."
"22392","(22392) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Muadh, on the authority of Tawus, who said: It is a sin."
"22393","(22393) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Mu’adh came from Yemen with a lightning rod during the time of Abu Bakr. So Omar said to him: Give them to Abu Bakr. He said: Why should I give him my slaves? He said: So he went to his house and did not push them away, so he spent the night there and then the next morning, so he handed them over to Abu Bakr. Omar said to him: What did you think? He said: You saw me in what a sleeper sees, as if I were in a fire where I was sheltering, so you seized me and prevented me from entering it. I thought they were the slaves, so Abu Bakr said: They are yours. When he went to his house, he stood up to pray and saw them. They would pray behind him. He said: To whom are you praying? They said: For God’s sake. He said: Go for God’s sake."
"22394","(22394) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hamid Al-Sa’idi: That the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Ibn al-Lutbibi took over the alms of Banu Sulaym. When he came, he said: This is for you and this is given as a gift. So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, got up and addressed the people, thanking God and praising Him. Then he said: What is the matter with the men whom we entrust? matters from which God has assigned us, then one of you comes and says: This is for you, and this was given to me. So will he not sit in it? His father’s house, or his mother’s house until a gift comes to him, if he is truthful. (Bukhari 1500 and Muslim 1463)"
"22395","(22395) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Adiy bin Umayrah Al-Kindi, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: Who among you whom We have appointed for a work, then We have concealed a hand-written one or more. He was a deceiver, and he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection. Then a black man from the Ansar stood up to him, as if I was looking at him, and said: O Messenger. God, accept your deeds from me. He said: What is that? He said: I heard you saying such-and-such. He said: So I say to him now: Whoever of you whom We appoint to do a job should bring us a little. And many of them, and whatever he was given he took, and whatever he was forbidden he refrained from. (Muslim 30. Abu Dawud 3576)"
"22396","(22396) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Ubaid Al-Tai narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’i: That Ali employed a man From the Banu Asad, he was called: Dubai’ bin Zuhair, or Zuhayr bin Duba’i’. When he came, he said: O Amir. Believers, certain things have been given to me in my work, and I have brought them to you. If they are lawful, you may eat them. Otherwise, I brought it to you, but Ali seized it and said: If I had kept it, it would have been deceit."
"22397","(22397) Ibn Abi Zaydi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abi Al-Khattab, on the authority of Abi Zur’i, on the authority of Abi Idris, on the authority of Thawban, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cursed the one who gives a bribe, the one who takes a bribe, and the one who takes a bribe, meaning the one who walks between them.\n(Ahmad 5/279. Bazzar 1353)"
"22398","(22398) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of his maternal uncle Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the briber and the bribe taker.\n(Tirmidhi 1337 and Abu Dawud 3575)"
"22399","(22399) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Umair, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: When the Prophet was sent May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Ibn Rawahhi went to the people of Khaybar and they presented gifts to him, so he returned it and said: It is permissible."
"22400","(22400) Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Umair, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: Umar wrote to the people of Iraq: We have gifts from our companions."
"22401","(22401) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Both the briber and the bribed are cursed."
"22402","(22402) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Hani’, he said: Abu Hudhayfy told me, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Alqamiya, said: A Thaqif delegation came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they brought him a gift, and he said: Is it a gift or is it truthful? They said: A gift. He said: A gift is sought by it to please the Messenger and fulfill a need, and by it charity is sought. By the face of God, they said: No, but rather a gift, so he accepted it from them, and they kept him busy for the afternoon prayer until he prayed the afternoon prayer.\n(Nasa’i 6593. Abu Ubaid 1770)"
"22403","(22403) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to kiss The gift is better than that. (Bukhari 2585. Abu Dawud 3530)"
"22404","(22404) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Misra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Guide those who do not guide you, and promise those who do not promise you."
"22405","(22405) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, who said: Abdullah bin Buraydah narrated to me, on the authority of his father: When Salman came to Medina, he brought a gift to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a plate and placed it in his hand. He said: What is this? He said: He gave charity to you and your companions. He said: I do not eat charity. So he took it away, then he brought it to him the next day with something like it, and he said: What? This? He said: This is a gift for you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his companions: Eat. (Tirmidhi 21. Hakim 16)"
"22406","(22406) Marwan narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid, who said: Umar said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace. He gives me the gift, so I say: O Messenger of God, give it to someone who is more in need of it than me. So the Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Take it and either finance it, or give it in charity, and whatever this money comes to you while you He is neither a beggar nor a supervisor, take him, and what not, do not follow him yourself. (Bukhari 1473, Muslim 723)"
"22407","(22407) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Hisham bin Saad told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Omar Ibn Al-Khattab says: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me money, which I returned. When I brought it to him, he said: What made you want to return it? I sent it to you. He said: You said to me, O Messenger of God: It is better for you not to take from the people. He said: That is only to ask the people. Whatever comes to you other than as a request, it is only a provision that God has bestowed upon you."
"22408","(22408) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amara: that Al-Aswad presented a camel to Sharih and he accepted it."
"22409","(22409) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: That Shurayh gave a camel to the lion. He asked Alqamah and said: What do you see? He said: Your brother has honored you. I think you should accept it. So he accepted it."
"22410","(22410) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, he said: Perhaps Abu Al-Haytham gave Ibrahim the camel made of reeds. So he accepts it."
"22411","(22411) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, saying: Tala’ was given to Ibrahim, and it was sweet, so he threw it away."
"22412","(22412) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Usama bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: “Educate one another and the greed will go away. Shake hands and the greed will go away.”"
"22413","(22413) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Yasir bin Amr, on the authority of his father: that Uwais Al-Qarani was naked and my father clothed him and kissed him."
"22414","(22414) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Muzam, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Wasi’ al-Azdi, who said: This money is not good except for those who Four things: a share of the Muslims, or a lawful trade, or a gift from a Muslim brother out of the back of his hand, or an inheritance in The Book of God"
"22415","(22415) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: Concerning a man to whom two men offered money, One of them is a Muslim brother, and the other is a relative of the Sultan. Which of them should he accept? He said: From relatives."
"22416","(22416) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Abu Darda’ said: If one of you joins his brother, let him accept. If he is in need of it, let him spend on it, and if he does not need it, let him give it to the people of need."
"22417","(22417) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, who said: A woman gave birth to a boy for Al-Musayyab, so he bought him a pair of sheep, so he sent Bye bye God"
"22418","(22418) Omar bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Do not reject the gift, respond to the supplicant, and do not strike the Muslims. (Bukhari 2568. Ahmad 2/479)"
"22419","(22419) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If an arm were offered to me, I would accept it, and if I were called to a handful of arms, I would respond."
"22420","(22420) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: Whoever asks of God, they will give him, and whoever gives you a sheep, accept him."
"22421","(22421) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Qurayh al-Kindi, on the authority of Salman, He said: I brought a gift to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a plate, and he said to his companions: Eat. (Ahmad 5/438, Tabarani 6155)"
"22422","(22422) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of a sheikh, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes. The gift is in the hands of the pilgrim. (Tabarani 2903)"
"22423","(22423) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, he heard Jabir bin Zaid say: We did not find in that time anything more beneficial for us. We have bribes."
"22424","(22424) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Umays narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman: That when Ibn Masoud came to the land The Abyssinian was seized for something and was given two dinars until he was released."
"22425","(22425) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Make your possessions a jinn without Your religion, and do not make your religion a paradise without an owner."
"22426","(22426) Hisham told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’. On the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd and Al-Sha’bi, that they said: There is no harm in a man doing something for himself. And his money if he fears injustice."
"22427","(22427) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, the same thing."
"22428","(22428) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He did not see any harm in a man giving some of his wealth. He preserves his honor through it."
"22429","(22429) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: Abdullah said: He who consumes usury. And the one who eats it is the same."
"22430","(22430) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Your kingdom, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hanzala bin Al-Rahib, on the authority of Ka’b Al-Ahbar, he said: Because I committed adultery thirty-three times. Fornication is more beloved to me than eating a dirham as interest. God knows that I ate it when I ate it while it was interest. (Ahmad 5/225)"
"22431","(22431) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdullah, he said: Abdullah said: God: The one who consumes usury and the one who gives it are the same, and the one who writes it and the one who witnesses it when they know about it, and the one who gives it and the one who receives it is equal to the good, and the Levite. Charity, and the apostate Bedouin after his migration is cursed, according to the words of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"22432","(22432) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was closed. The gates of usury are upon you, and you are seeking its prohibitions."
"22433","(22433) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Cursed are the one who consumes usury, the one who pays it, the one who writes it, and the one who witnesses it."
"22434","(22434) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Murā al-Hamdani, he said: `Umar said: Three Because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, explained them to us more beloved to me than the world and what is in it: disagreement and disagreement. And usury.\n(Ibn Majah 2727. Hakim 304)"
"22435","(22435) Waki’ narrated to us, Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: I heard Al-Nu’man bin Bashir deliver a sermon and he took refuge. With his two fingers to his ears, he says: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The lawful is clear and the forbidden is clear. And between them there are doubtful matters, so whoever fears the doubtful things will be clear in his religion and honor, and whoever falls into the doubtful things will fall into the forbidden, Like a shepherd who grazes around a wilderness and is about to graze therein. Indeed, every angel has a fever, and God protects his tissues. Indeed, And there is a piece of flesh in the body. If it is sound, the whole body is sound, and if it is spoiled, the whole body is spoiled. Except for the weakness of the heart.\n(Bukhari 520 Muslim 1220)"
"22436","(22436) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, who said: There is a usury more severe in the sight of God Almighty than Thirty-six fornications."
"22437","(22437) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Usury is seventy times the easiest of which is a man’s marriage to his mother, and the worst of usury is prolonged. A man in honor of his brother. (Bukhari 239)"
"22438","(22438) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hani’, on the authority of Amir, who said: I read the book of the people of Najran and found In it, if you consume usury, there will be no reconciliation between us and you, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not reconciling with one who eats. Usury"
"22439","(22439) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: “Those who consume usury will not stand except Just as the one whom Satan has caused to stumble because of his touch will rise. (Ibn Jarir 102)"
"22440","(22440) His youth narrated to us, he said: Shu’ba narrated to us, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abi Juhaif, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet was cursed. May God bless him and grant him peace, the one who consumes usury and the one who pays it. (Bukhari 2086)"
"22441","(22441) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath and Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Omar delivered a speech, thanked God and praised him, then He said: We command you to do things that perhaps they are not suitable for you, and we forbid you things that perhaps they are not suitable for you, and another The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not promise us the signs of usury, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested and did not explain them. For us, it is only usury and riba, so leave what doubts you for what does not doubt you.\n When Al-Shaabi was asked about something, he would say: It is only usury and riba, so they left usury and doubtful matters. (Ahmad 1/36)"
"22442","(22442) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Issa bin Al-Mughiryah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Omar said: I was afraid that we might We have increased usury tenfold out of fear of it."
"22443","(22443) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Ansari was given to a boy. He had four thousand, so he joined Asbaan and ran until there were twenty thousand, then he perished, and it was said to him: He was a slave. Usury, so he took four thousand and left anything else."
"22444","(22444) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid al-Ansari, he said: Abd said: God: Usury has seventy-four chapters, and polytheism is like that."
"22445","(22445) Yahya bin Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Abu Ya’four, on the authority of Ayman, he said: I heard Ali saying: I heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Whoever takes land without its rights is required to carry its soil to the gathering place.\n(Ahmad 4/172, Ibn Hibban 5164)"
"22446","(22446) Ibn Abi Zayd told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Zayd, he said: I heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Whoever takes an inch of the earth unjustly, it will encircle him from seven earths.\n(Bukhari 3198 and Muslim 1231)"
"22447","(22447) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abi Amr Al-Shaybani, he said: I was informed that no one He steals land, and there will be repentance for him as long as he finds no land to dig."
"22448","(22448) Khalid ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Bilal, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever takes a span of land will be surrounded on the Day of Resurrection by Seven earths. (Muslim 43 Ahmad 2/388)"
"22449","(22449) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, he said: I was sitting with Ali. Then a man came to him and said: Did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, make secrets to you? He became angry and said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would never confide to me anything that people kept secret, except that he told me something. With four words, he said: What are they? He said: May God curse the one who curses his father, and may God curse the one who slaughters for someone other than God, and may God curse the one who harbors a new prophet, and may God curse the one who changes The lighthouse of the earth.\n(Bukhari 17 Ahmad 1/118)"
"22450","(22450) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ash'ari said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The greatest deception in the sight of God on the Day of Resurrection is an cubit of land. A man steals it from another, and the two neighbors have the land between them, so one of them steals it from his friend, and he is surrounded by seven Two lands (Ahmad 341. Tabarani 3463)"
"22451","(22451) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed four people: Whoever takes refuge in someone other than Allah, whoever shelters a newly-invented person, whoever disobeys his parents, and whoever steals a lighthouse, he said: I said: What is a lighthouse? He said: A man takes from his owner’s land into his own land."
"22452","(22452) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara ibn Umair, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Whoever oppresses a span of land So the creatures of the earth surrounded him on the Day of Resurrection, but they would not bear him."
"22453","(22453) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Kurayb, on the authority of Kurayb, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, saying: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Cursed is he who destroys anything from the borders of the earth without its right.\n(Ahmad 1/217. Ibn Hibban 4417)"
"22454","(22454) Yahya bin Abi Zaidah told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata, who said: We have been informed that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The believers are subject to their conditions. (Tirmidhi 1352. Abu Dawud 3589)"
"22455","(22455) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Khaled ibn Muhammad, on the authority of a sheikh from Banu Kinanah, who said: I heard Omar says: The Muslim is with his police."
"22456","(22456) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Muslims are on their terms unless May God disobey you"
"22457","(22457) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Shabib bin Gharqadiya, he said, I heard a narrator saying: For every Muslim Condition"
"22458","(22458) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, saying: A woman came to Al-Sha’bi and said: My daughter was sold on the condition that she would not be sold. He said: Your daughter is on her condition."
"22459","(22459) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Nasir bin Dhu’luq Al-Thawri, on the authority of Amr bin Rashid Al-Ashja’i: A man bought a sick camel from a man, and the seller removed its skin and the camel was healed. So they disputed with Omar and he sent them. To Ali, and Ali said: The camel is led in the market, and it will have the freshness of its skin."
"22460","(22460) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: He has a share."
"22461","(22461) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Zaid: Concerning a man who sold a camel to another man. He cut off his head and said to him: “Shaw the head.”"
"22462","(22462) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: A man sold a sick camel to another man and set its head as a stipend. He caught it, and the camel was healed, but he did not slaughter it. Shurayh said to him: Give him his share. So I mentioned it to Amir, and he said: He has judged me. And a slice of sharwi."
"22463","(22463) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: Muslims are on their terms."
"22464","(22464) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Ghanam said: Omar said: Rights are granted under conditions."
"22465","(22465) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do not quarrel, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, and be servants of God as brothers.\n(Bukhari 408. Ahmad 2/501)"
"22466","(22466) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of the Awwam, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Saksaki, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: I heard him say: The defiant person who consumes usury is a traitor."
"22467","(22467) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Saksaki, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, the same."
"22468","(22468) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not argue. (Bukhari 2140, Muslim 51)"
"22469","(22469) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: Najsh is not permissible."
"22470","(22470) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Mu’allim narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: I told Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Layla: He told me a hadith in which the chapters on usury are collected for me. He said: Do not eat if you have seen something that is not due to you. Guarantee"
"22471","(22471) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Prophet was sent May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Attab bin Asid was sent to the people of Mecca, and he said: Do you know where I sent you? I have sent you to the people of God. Then he said: It is about four things: about a sale and a loan, about two conditions in a sale, and about a profit unless Guaranteed, and from selling what you do not have.\n(Abu Dawud 3498, An-Nasa’i 6227)"
"22472","(22472) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib: That his grandfather was, when he was sent He forbade them from trade, from a loan and from a sale, from two conditions in a sale, and from a profit that they did not guarantee."
"22473","(22473) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yaqoub ibn al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Marouf ibn Sa’d: that Jabir ibn Zayd borrowed a silk in A fine befell them."
"22474","(22474) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the eye if it is in good condition."
"22475","(22475) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim. On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi. And Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim, they said: There is no harm in the evil eye."
"22476","(22476) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Qurayr, he said: Ibn Sirin was asked about The eye? He said: The man used to take his belongings to the market, and he would sell them for cash and sell them for cash."
"22477","(22477) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Ka’b Abd Rabbā ibn Ubaid narrated to us, saying: I asked Ibn Sirin about selling Silk? He said: The man used to buy goods and then put them away. If he found a profit for the money, he would sell it, and if he found a profit for the women, he would sell it. He sold it"
"22478","(22478) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Aflah, he said: I said to Al-Qasim: The man is asking me for wheat and oil, but not Is it that he knew the price of it, or I knew it and bought it, then sold it to him for a specified period? He said: Yes."
"22479","(22479) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: Take a mortgage on the property."
"22480","(22480) Waki’ told us, he said: Badr bin Hawizah told us, he said: I asked Al-Sha’abi about the mortgage on the property? He said: There is no harm in it."
"22481","(22481) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Marzuq al-Taymi, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said regarding the mortgage in Al-Ainah: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died and his armor was mortgaged."
"22482","(22482) Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak: He hated it."
"22483","(22483) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’ Al-Kaili, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: Do not buy fish in water, for it is deception."
"22484","(22484) Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Ayash, narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He hated his next blow."
"22485","(22484) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim: He hated hitting him. The sniper"
"22486","(22484) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir and Ata’: They disliked selling stones."
"22487","(22485) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim: He disliked selling stones."
"22488","(22486) Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hammad: Omar bin Abdul Aziz granted permission to sell stones."
"22489","(22489) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The services of the manager are not sold except to the one who Himself"
"22490","(22490) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Qaridh bin Shayba, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: There is no harm in serving the manager, and Al-Zuhri used to say it."
"22491","(22491) Waki` narrated to us, Hammad bin Zaid said: On the authority of Ayoub al-Sakhtiyani and Yahya bin Ateeq, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: There is no harm in selling the servants of the manager from Himself"
"22492","(22492) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus: That two men among them had a boy, so they freed him to serve them. As long as they lived, one of them bought his friend’s share from the other. Ibn Sirin was asked about that, but he did not see any harm in it."
"22493","(22493) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sold May God bless him and grant him peace. His servants are mastermind. (Bayhaqi 312)"
"22494","(22494) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you enter the Muslim market, buy what you find, unless You know that it is betrayal or theft."
"22495","(22495) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Muhammad, on the authority of a man from the people of Medina, who said: ?? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever buys a stolen item knowing that he has stolen it, has shared in its shame and sin.\n(Hakim 35. Bayhaqi 335)"
"22496","(22496) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I said to Ubaidah: I buy the stolen goods while I know. Is it theft? He said: No, I said: So did he buy treason when I know that it is treason? He said: No, I said: So should I buy the work? He said: Can you leave it?\n(22496)"
"22497","(22497) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, with something similar."
"22498","(22498) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad: He used to dislike the broker’s wage unless it was a known wage."
"22499","(22499) Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: What a present person does not sell. Felt? He said: He is not a broker."
"22500","(22500) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim and Ibn Sirin, they said: There is no harm in receiving a reward. If the broker buys hand to hand,"
"22501","(22501) Waki’ told us, he said: Laith Abu Abd al-Aziz told us, he said: I asked Ata’ about brokerage, and he said: There is no problem. With it"
"22502","(22502) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan hated brokerage."
"22503","(22503) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad: Is there an intercessor for the servant? They said: No."
"22504","(22504) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, he said: He decided The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used intercession in everything. (Tirmidhi 1371)"
"22505","(22505) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He used to say: There is no Shafi’i in animals."
"22506","(22506) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amara, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Aban bin Uthman, He said: Othman said: There is no pre-emption for a well, nor for a stallion, and the hills cut off all pre-emption. (Malik 717. Abdul Razzaq 14426)"
"22507","(22507) Waki’ told us, he said: Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajli told us, he said: I asked Ata’: Is there an intercessor for the garment? He said: Yes."
"22508","(22508) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan ibn Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, Ibn Shubramah, and Rabi’ah. Opinion, they said about two men with a bag between them, so this one says: I have part of it, and this one says: I have all of it.\n Ibn Shubrumah said: To the one who said: He is all mine, half of it purely, and it will be what remains between them.\n Ibn Abi Layla said: one-third and two-thirds.\n Rabi`ah said: It is two halves between them."
"22509","(22509) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith: There are two men who have money between them, so one of them claims half of it, and the other claims two-thirds. He said: He gives the owner of the two-thirds half of the money, because the owner of the half has been absolved of the half, and he gives the one who claims the half a third, because The owner of the two-thirds has been released from the third, and what remains is one-sixth, so they both claim it, so between them they are two halves."
"22510","(22510) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: The mortgage is not sold except when... Sultan"
"22511","(22511) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, who said: Muhammad ibn Sirin sent me to Ias ibn Mu'awiyah, who was in charge of the judge, said: Tell him: I have a pawned yarn that I fear will spoil, so he commanded me to I sell it"
"22512","(22512) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: He used to monopolize The oil"
"22513","(22513) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Muslim Al-Khabbat, he said: I was buying for Sa’id bin The musayyab has the nuclear, the non-permanent, and the khatt, so he monopolizes it."
"22514","(22514) Ibn Abi Zayd and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If a woman spends from her husband’s house without spoiling it, she will have her reward. And he has the same for what he has earned, and he has the same for what he has spent, and the treasurer has the same as that.\nAbu Muawiyah added: Without detracting from their wages in any way. (Bukhari 1425. Muslim 710)"
"22515","(22515) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I asked him. A woman said: The poor person is coming. Should I give alms from my husband’s money without his permission? He thought of her and said to her: May he not give your jewelery in charity without your permission."
"22516","(22516) Yahya bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: No. A woman should give charity only from her own means, but as for her husband’s wealth, it is not permissible for her to give it except with his permission, and the reward will be between them."
"22517","(22517) Yahya bin Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Al-Salt bin Bahram, on the authority of Umm Salih: A woman said to Aisha: Is it permissible for a woman to take anything from her husband’s house without his permission? She said: What is wrong with her if she did that or broke into her neighbour's house and stole?"
"22518","(22518) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Hind came to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man, so he will not give me anything. It is sufficient for me and my children, except for what I took from his wealth while he did not know. So he said: Take what is sufficient for you and your children on an honorable basis. (Bukhari 2211. Ahmad 6/39)"
"22519","(22519) Waki’ told us, he said: Iyas bin Daghfal told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God, what is the matter with me and my companion? He said: What is the matter with you? He said: You give alms from my house without my permission. He said: The reward is between you. He said: What do you think if I prevent her? He said to him?? Whatever you expect, but you are not stingy with it. (Abdul Razzaq 14616)"
"22520","(22520) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jubayr, on the authority of Saad, who said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and the women. A distinguished woman came up to him as if she were one of the women of Mudar, and said: O Messenger of God, we are all burdened by him. Our fathers, our wives, and our children, what is permissible for us of their wealth? He said: You may eat fresh dates or give them to yourself as gifts. (Abu Dawud 1683, Hakim 134)"
"22521","(22521) Ismail bin Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Muslim, who said: I heard Abu Imamah Al-Bailili saying: I heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in his Hajj in the year of the Farewell Hajj: A woman should not spend anything from her husband’s house except With His permission, it was said: O Messenger of God, not even food? He said: This is the best of our wealth."
"22522","(22522) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Muhammad, and Shuraih, who said: Selling to a partner is permissible unless Here it is"
"22523","(22523) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Every partner who sells to him in his company is permissible except A partner in an inheritance."
"22524","(22524) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Suwayd bin Qays, he said: I and his two companions were brought. Al-Abdi bought fine clothes from Hijr, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to us and bargained with us for trousers, and we had a weigher who weighed for a reward. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Weigh, weigh and weigh.” (Tirmidhi 1305, Abu Dawud 3329)"
"22525","(22525) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, bought from me He, peace be upon him, delivered a camel, so its price was weighed for me, and it was swung to me. (Bukhari 3089. Ahmad 3/302)"
"22526","(22526) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a debt. He fulfilled me and increased me. (Bukhari 443. Ahmad 3/319)"
"22527","(22527) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: I had a debt on Al-Hasan bin Ali, so I went to him. I sued him, and I found him coming out of the bathroom with henna on his nails, and his maid was rubbing the henna off of him with a bottle. So he called for a bag containing dirhams and said: Take this. I said: This is more than you are entitled to. He said: Take it. So I took it and found it. It is sixty or seventy dirhams more than my right."
"22528","(22528) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in preferring Weight"
"22529","(22529) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Al-Khattab, on the authority of Abu Zur’i, on the authority of Abu Idris, on the authority of Thawban, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the one who bribes, the one who takes a bribe, and the one who bribes, meaning the one who walks. Between them."
"22530","(22530) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of his maternal uncle Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Salamah, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the briber and the bribe taker."
"22531","(22531) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Shurayh, he said: The briber and the bribe-taker, And the slanderer.\n Waki` said: He means the slanderer who says: He bribed the judge."
"22532","(22532) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi al-Najjoud, on the authority of Zur bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Ibn Masoud. He said: Bribery is unlawful."
"22533","(22533) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham: Concerning a man who pledged a slave. So he freed him, saying: Emancipating a slave is permissible and the mortgager follows the mortgagee."
"22534","(22534) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: I asked Al-Hasan bin Salih and a partner about a man who took a bet on his servant, then Will he free him? They said: His emancipation is permissible.\n A partner said: The servant strives for the mortgaged one.\n Al-Hasan bin Salih said: He is not obligated to seek."
"22535","(22535) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning a man who bought a slave from a man and did not take possession of him until He emancipated him, he said: It is not permissible to emancipate him until he seizes him or redeems him."
"22536","(22536) Waki` narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan say: If a man frees his slave, he will be freed from the mortgage, and if he returns it, he will be freed. From the mortgage, and if it is a mother and he has intercourse with her and she gives birth to a child, then she leaves the mortgage, and if the master is well-off, he follows the mortgager. The master takes the mortgage, and if he is insolvent, they strive for less than their value and the mortgage.\n Sufyan said: He returns what he strove to the master if he is able, but the mother of the child and the one who managed it do not return to their master. With something, because their service is for the Master."
"22537","(22537) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He did not see any harm in the two men. They join together, and one comes with dinars and the other with dirhams, and he says: The dinars are the same thing as all of it. So if they wanted to They separated, the owner of the dinars took dinars, and the owner of the dirhams took dirhams, then they divided the profit.\n Hisham said: Muhammad loved to have dirhams and dirhams, and dinars and dinars."
"22538","(22538) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I saw Shurayh making a judgement, and with him was Abu Amr Al-Shaybani and similar sheikhs who sit with him in the judiciary."
"22539","(22539) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Muharib bin Dathar, Hammad, Al-Hakam, and one of them on the authority of One on his right and the other on his left, looking at Al-Hakam once, and at Hammad once, and the opponents are in his hands."
"22540","(22540) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: Al-Qasim said to me: Sit with me while he judges among the people."
"22541","(22541) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, bought carrots from a Bedouin with an wasq of dates, so he sent them to his maternal uncle, Bint Hakim. So she paid him in full, and he said: The best of you are the faithful and the good ones.\n(Ahmad 6/268)"
"22542","(22542) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bought The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the man: Go and tell them: You eat until you are satisfied, and you eat until you are satisfied. Meaning: the measure, so the man came out scratching his elbows. It means: it increases. (Abu Dawud 169)"
"22543","(22543) Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No mother is sanctified. The weak in her will not be given his due unless he is oppressed. (Abu Ali) 1091)"
"22544","(22544) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, who said: I witnessed Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman and a working man disputed over me. One of the pilgrims’ workers seized food that was his own, so Al-Qasim asked him for the evidence, and he brought his evidence, and they testified that he had taken food for himself. From his homes, Al-Qasim said to them: How much food did he take? They said: We do not know what his measure was. He said: I will not judge him for anything until you tell me the measure of what he took of food."
"22545","(22545) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I witnessed it and he settled with me. Two men bought an animal, one of them, from the other. He said to the arbitrator: “Wait, let him give me a guarantor if he gives me this animal.” He said: Did you stipulate that when you made the sale? He said: No. He said: You are not allowed to do that."
"22546","(22546) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Jamil bin Bishr, who said: I saw Salem bin Abdullah pass by the companion of Sair, meaning We cooked it, so he took some of it and tasted it, and said: How do you sell this?"
"22547","(22547) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no problem if a man buys To eat from the fruit means to taste it."
"22548","(22548) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm if he buys the thing. He tastes it before he buys it."
"22549","(22549) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith. And Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi. And Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who sells goods for cash, then buys them for less than he sold them for before. To criticize his idea."
"22550","(22550) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: There is no harm if he sells it for cash. To buy it without what he sold it for, if he pays it back."
"22551","(22551) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, who said: The kafala and the hawala are the same."
"22552","(22552) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He saw no harm in pure flasks with a weighing scale. The broken one, if it is better than the clean one.\nIbn Sirin disliked that, except in a weight for a weight."
"22553","(22553) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They do not resemble two young men. Milk to sell. (Abdul Razzaq 7270)"
"22554","(22554) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim: He disliked the dirham being broken when The grocer takes something other than what he broke."
"22555","(22555) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: He used to hate hastening the dirhams. To the grocer, and he was asked about that handsome man? He said: By God, this has never happened to us."
"22556","(22556) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: Concerning a man who hands over dirhams to a grocer. He said: No. He takes only what he has surrendered to, and if he leaves it with him, he may take whatever he wants."
"22557","(22557) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad: He hated the grocer to give him the dirham, so he took it. It is sold from him, but it is taken from him, so when a dirham is complete, he gives it to him."
"22558","(22558) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever buys an Egyptian property has the option of it. If he wishes, he may return it and return with it a Saa’ of Dates\n(Bukhari 2148, Abu Dawud 3436)"
"22559","(22559) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of a man from Companions of the Prophet, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever buys an Egyptian property will have one of two options for it, if he returns it. Return with it a saa of dates, or a saa of food. (Ahmad 4/314)"
"22560","(22560) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Taymimi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, he said: Abdullah said: Whoever buys a gift and sells it back, let him return a saa with it."
"22561","(22561) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, he said: I asked him about the Khas whose family called him This is this house and the people of this. He said: It is for the one on whom the swaddle is worn. And I asked him about the brick wall that the people of this house call it and the people of this one. He said: It is for those who are fair."
"22562","(22562) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Humaid, who said: I went with my father to Shurayh and I heard him judge. Especially to the one who has swaddling clothes."
"22563","(22563) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He hated it, one who tyers with tyers. It means debt for debt."
"22564","(22564) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hakam: He hated a term for a future, meaning: a debt. Obese"
"22565","(22565) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Aslam Al-Munqari, on the authority of Ata’: He hated it sooner or later. It means: debt for debt."
"22566","(22566) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of a pearl for a pound, meaning: a debt for a debt. (Daraqutni 71, Hakim 57)"
"22567","(22567) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa: That his father was He sells juice."
"22568","(22568) Waki` narrated to us, Shu`ba said: On the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Aqar bin al-Mughiriya bin Shu`ba, he said Ibn Umar was asked about selling a vineyard? He said: Zabubu, then they sold it."
"22569","(22569) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan ibn Dinar, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Sa’d: The owner of Sa’d’s estate came to him and said: The grapes had increased, so he said: Take raisins. He sold them grapes, and he said: There were more than that. He said: So Saad went out to She lost it, so he ordered it to be removed, and he said to Qaramaniah: I will not trust you with anything after that."
"22570","(22570) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn: That Abu Ubaidah had a vineyard, and he used to say: To his agents: sell him grapes, but if he does not buy them, sell him juice when you press them."
"22571","(22571) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab. On the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in selling juice as long as it does not boil."
"22572","(22572) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning a man who sells juice to someone who turns it into wine. He said: I would love for him to sell it to someone else who would make it wine, and if he sold it, there is no problem."
"22573","(22573) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He was asked about selling juice, and he said: Sell whatever is sweet."
"22574","(22574) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of the ruling: Concerning a man who has a vineyard and sells it juice. He said: If he sells it juice or grapes, there is no problem."
"22575","(22575) Wakī’ narrated to us, Al-Hasan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Tawq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Do not sell grapes to someone who makes them Wine"
"22576","(22576) Waki’ told us, he said: I asked Sufyan about selling juice? He said: Sell what is permissible from whomever you wish."
"22577","(22577) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Do not sell juice from someone who makes it. Wine"
"22578","(22578) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mu’mar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: That ‘Umar made a decree regarding a man who gave to another man. Bhima gave birth. He said: He has the right to return with the money on the day he was blessed."
"22579","(22579) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ziyad, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote That he would return the gift on the day he was gifted, and write, “Indeed, the increase is for the one to whom it was given.”"
"22580","(22580) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Whoever swears an oath to be patient in order to seize the property of a Muslim man and therewith he is an immoral person, he will meet God and He will be upon him. Angry, he said: Then Al-Ash'ath bin Qays entered and said: What is Abu Abd al-Rahman telling you? We said, such and such. He said: He spoke the truth. By God, it was revealed. There were opponents between me and a Jewish man, so I disputed with him. To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do you have a clear proof? I said: No. He said: You have his oath. I said: Then he will swear. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever swears an oath will be patient. So he mentioned a parable of the words of Abdullah, and these verses were revealed: {Indeed, those who buy the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price}"
"22581","(22581) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b ibn Malik: He heard his brother Abdullah bin Ka’b narrated that Abu Umamah Al-Harithi narrated to him that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: No. A man cuts off a Muslim man’s right with his oath, except that God has forbidden the jinn for him and made Hell fire for him. He said: Then a man from The people: O Messenger of God, even if it is a small thing. He said: Even if it is a siwak from your ear. (Muslim 219. Ahmad 5/260)"
"22582","(22582) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Hashim bin Hashim told us, he said: Abdullah bin Nastas informed me: He heard Jabir Ibn Abdullah says: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No one shall swear at this pulpit on the oath of a sinner, even if On a green siwak, unless he takes his place in the Fire, or the Fire is required for him. (Abu Dawud 3241, Ibn Majah 2325)"
"22583","(22583) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Jami’, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Whoever seizes a Muslim’s wealth unjustly with his right hand will meet God while He is angry with him. (Bukhari 7445. Muslim 123)"
"22584","(22584) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Thabit bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of his father On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: If he cuts it off with his right hand, he is among those to whom God does not speak, nor does he look. To them, and He will not purify them, and they will have a painful punishment. (Ahmad 4/394)"
"22585","(22585) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Alqamah bin Wael, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he said: If he swears about his wealth that he will eat it unjustly, he will meet God while he is turning away from it. (Muslim 1231, Abu Dawud 3239)"
"22586","(22586) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Harith bin Sulaiman Al-Kindi narrated to us, on the authority of Kurdous Al-Thaalabi, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Qais, who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Whoever swears an oath to be patient in order to have the property of a Muslim taken for it, while in it he is an immoral person. He met God while he was a leper. (Abu Dawud 3238. Ahmad 5/212)"
"22587","(22587) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Thawr narrated to us, on the authority of Mahfouz bin Alqami, on the authority of Abu al-Darda`, he said: Whoever swears an oath on The right word of an unseen person who committed a sin in it, who spoke the truth in it, or committed an act of wrongdoing in it."
"22588","(22588) Yunus narrated to us, saying: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid bin Al-Mujair. Bin Qunfud, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al Ansari, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Unais, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: He did not swear He swore an oath to God to be patient, and He entered into it like a mosquito’s wing, except that it would remain a mark in his heart until the Day of Resurrection.\n(Tirmidhi 3020, Ahmad 3/495)"
"22589","(22589) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: Whoever swears an oath as a patient and willful liar, let him repent. In front of him is his abode in the Fire. (Abu Dawud 3240, Ahmad 4/436)"
"22590","(22590) Shababi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zaid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: Whoever takes the oath of a Muslim to cut it off, he will not be blessed. Therein\n(Ahmad 1/1888 Abu Ali 951)"
"22591","(22591) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, on the authority of Imran al-Qattan, who said: I heard al-Hasan being asked about a man who saw his neighbor in The market is being sold, and she said: It is stolen, and he said: It is bought, and not given in charity. I asked his leaders about that."
"22592","(22592) Abu Bakr ibn Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If his servant writes and he has a servant or His mother, then it is part of writing to him, but if he has a son and he conceals them, then he does not have that."
"22593","(22593) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, something similar."
"22594","(22594) Muhammad bin Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I told him: A man wrote a slave to him or He boycotted him, so he withheld from him any property of his own: a slave, a kind, or other property? He said: It is for the servant, and Amr bin Dinar and Suleiman bin Musa said it."
"22595","(22595) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The mother of his sons and his sons will all enter into Writing to him"
"22596","(22596) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad: That a man wrote a servant of his and stipulated his loyalty. And his inheritance and his estate. When he fulfilled his obligation, he was freed. Then he died, and his guardians disputed over his inheritance, and the share was invalidated. Then the master said: What is the use of a policeman for me for twenty years? Shurayh said: God’s condition accepted your condition fifty years ago."
"22597","(22597) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid: That Adiy wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz about a man who wrote to his servant. And he made a condition for him to make a share of his inheritance, so he wrote to him: No one has a condition to reduce or take away anything from the obligations of God."
"22598","(22598) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ was asked about a man who wrote, and stipulated that his family Do we have a share of your inheritance? He said: No, God’s condition came before their condition."
"22599","(22599) Suwayd bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Awan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: similar to what Ata’ said."
"22600","(22600) Abdou and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: He hated the reward Al-Mughniyah, his servant added: And he said, “I do not like to eat it.”"
"22601","(22601) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He disliked the reward of a mourner and a singer."
"22602","(22602) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim: He disliked the reward of a mourner. And the singer and the soothsayer."
"22603","(22603) Ja’far ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Hubayra (and all of them are unlawful acts) He said: The dowry of prostitution, and the soothsayer did not take it for granted."
"22604","(22604) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in buying the instrument. By disguising a man whether he intended it or not."
"22605","(22605) Waki’ told us, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I asked him about a man who bought from a man a check in which Three dinars for a garment. He said: It is not suitable."
"22606","(22606) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi: He hated it and said: He deceived him."
"22607","(22607) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If it becomes clear that a man is bankrupt, it is not permissible for him to be freed and he is in charge of it. A debt, and if it is not clear that he is bankrupt, then emancipating him is permissible."
"22608","(22608) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Raba’i, who said: He narrated to me. Abu Al-Yusr said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever looks after a distressed person or provides relief for him: God will shade him in a shade. His throne\n(Muslim 74, Hakim 28)"
"22609","(22609) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Yusr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted in a similar manner. (Tabarani 374)"
"22610","(22610) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: I heard Ubaid bin Umair, he said: He was a man who paid debts to people. And he sells allegiance to them, and he has a scribe and a reciprocater, so the one who is in difficulty and the one who is looking forward will come to him and say: Eat and reconsider and go beyond. Today, he ignores us. He said: He met God and no one had done good but He forgave him."
"22611","(22611) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Masoud, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: A man from among those before you was judged guilty, but nothing good was found for him, except that he was a wealthy man who mingled with people. So He said to His servants: “Forgive us for the one who is in difficulty.” And He said: “Allah to His angels: We are more deserving of that than Him.” So they forgave Him.\n(Muslim 30. Tirmidhi 1307)"
"22612","(22612) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Abu Masoud, in a similar manner, but he did not narrate it."
"22613","(22613) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Khutmi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abu Qatada said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: Whoever forgives his debtor or erases it from him, is in the shadow of The Throne on the Day of Resurrection. (Ahmad 5/300, Abd bin Humaid 195)"
"22614","(22614) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Raba’i, who said: Uqba said: Bin Amr Lahdhifi: Tell me something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: There was a man among those before you, to whom the angel came to take his soul and said: Have you done good? He said: I do not know him. He said: Look. He said: I do not know him except that I was a man who took risks with people and mingled with them, so I used to look. The one who is in difficulty and neglects the well-off, and God admits him to Paradise. He said afterward: And I heard him say that. (Muslim 1195)"
"22615","(22615) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Zuhayr bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sahl bin Hanif, that Sahl narrated to him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever helps Struggling in the path of God, or grieving in His hardship, or struggling in His neck, God will shade him on the Day when there is no shade but His shade."
"22616","(22616) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a Bedouin. He sells something and says: You have to pay the first price, or pay the first price, for the profit comes with tolerance. (Abu Dawud 167)"
"22617","(22617) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hussein, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: The master of the goods has more right to the price. (Abu Dawud 166)"
"22618","(22618) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: I will fill his nose with poison."
"22619","(22619) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Abu Bakr said in His illness in which he died: Look at what has increased in my wealth since I entered the caliphate, then send it to the Caliph after me. I used to make it permissible, and I had gained from your friendliness the same way as I had gained from trade. Aisha said: When We looked and saw a Nubian slave carrying her two young boys and a camel who was watering it for him. She said: So we sent them to Omar. She said: Then my grandfather told me that Omar cried and said: May God have mercy on Abu Bakr, he made those who came after him very tired."
"22620","(22620) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Abi Rashid, who said: Omar said: Were it not for these sales You have become superior to people."
"22621","(22621) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikiya, he said: Aisha said: Abu Bakr traded with Quraysh."
"22622","(22622) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Khaythamiya, he said: Abu Darda’ said: I was a merchant before The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent, I wanted to combine trade. And the servants did not treat me steadfastly, so I left my business and turned to the servants."
"22623","(22623) Waki’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed that Abu Bakr was a merchant. Quraysh"
"22624","(22624) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Qays, on the authority of Asim bin Abi al-Najjoud, on the authority of Abu Wael He said: A dirham of your trade is more beloved to me than a tenth of your gift."
"22625","(22625) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Farafsi, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever seeks this worldly life as lawful, refraining from asking and seeking He treats his family and is compassionate towards his neighbor. He will meet God and His face is like the moon on a full-moon night, and whoever seeks the world as lawful and hypocritical He met God while He was angry with Him. (Abdullah bin Hamid 1433. Bayhaqi 9890)"
"22626","(22626) Wakī’ narrated to us, he said: Amr bin Issa Abu Na’amă heard it, or he said: Harith bin Al-Rabi’ Al-Adawi narrated to us, He said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab saying: Three journeys have been prescribed for you: Hajj, Umrah, and jihad in the path of God. And a man strives with his wealth in one of these ways. I seek with my wealth God’s bounty that is dearer to me than dying on it. My bed, and if I had said: She is a witness, I would have seen that she is a witness."
"22627","(22627) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of his father, saying: I heard Amr bin Al-Aas saying: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: O Amr, strengthen your weapon and your clothing and come to me. He said: So I strengthened my weapon against you. And my clothes, then I came to him and found him performing ablution, so he looked up and looked at him and said: O Amr, I want to send you May God grant you peace and spoil you, and give you a good amount of wealth. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, I have not converted to Islam. Out of desire for money. I only embraced Islam out of desire for jihad and to be with you. He said: O Amr, be blessed with good money. For the good man. (Bukhari 2991, Ahmad 4/202)"
"22628","(22628) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Muzam narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’ al-Azdi, who said: This is not good. Money except from four things: a share for the ransom of Muslims, or lawful trade, or a gift from a Muslim brother out of back of hand, or An inheritance in the Book of God."
"22629","(22629) Waki` narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A caravan came He went to Medina, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, bought from it and made a small amount of money, so he divided it among the widows of Banu Abdul Muttalib. And he said: I will not buy anything that I do not have the price for. (Abu Dawud 3337. Ahmad 1/235)"
"22630","(22630) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Ayoub, who said: Abu Qalabi used to urge me to become professional. And demand, and Abu Qalabab said: Wealth comes from well-being."
"22631","(22631) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Mujahid: {Spend of the good things that you have earned}, He said: Trade."
"22632","(22632) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, as a narrator, He said: Indeed, an immoral oath is one spent for the sake of goods and one that is destroyed for one’s gain. (Bukhari 2087, Muslim 131)"
"22633","(22633) Zayd ibn Harun told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Ma’abad ibn Ka’b ibn Malik, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Beware of swearing too much, for it will be spent and then fulfilled.\n(Ahmad 5/297, Ibn Majah 2209)"
"22634","(22634) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Kathir, on the authority of Ma’abad ibn Ka’b ibn Malik, on the authority of Abu Qatada He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Beware of swearing too much in sales, for he will spend, then He is right"
"22635","(22635) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Talha narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jahadi, on the authority of Zazan, he said: It was Ali comes to the market and greets him, then he says: O merchants, beware of swearing too much when selling, for it is... He spends the goods and achieves the blessing."
"22636","(22636) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Salma bin Ziyad bin Akhi Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, On the authority of Salem, he said: Ibn Masoud said: Faith seals sales and secures earnings."
"22637","(22637) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Gharza, who said: We used to buy baskets. In Medina, and we used to call ourselves the brokers, so we came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave us a name better than We used to call ourselves by it, and he said: O merchants, this sale is attended by idle talk and swearing, so taint it with honesty.\n(Tirmidhi 1208 and Abu Dawud 3319)"
"22638","(22638) Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Samimi narrated to us, saying: Hatim bin Abi Saghira narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to the hadith of Qays bin Abi Gharza. (Bayhaqi 4848)"
"22639","(22639) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Bashar ibn Kadam al-Sulami, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Swearing is an oath, or one of regret."
"22640","(22440) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali ibn Mudrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Kharsha ibn al-Hurr, on the authority of Abu Dharr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There are three to whom God will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them. And for them is a painful punishment: the generous and the poor, and the one who spends his goods by false oaths. (Muslim 171. Abu Dawud 4084)"
"22641","(22641) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Ansari Council, who said: I heard Khalid bin Saad, the client of Abu Masoud, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah say: Lying is the salt of sales: it wastes the goods and destroys the profit."
"22642","(22642) Waki’ told us, he said: Thawr told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Saif, on the authority of Haram bin Hakim, he said: Umar bin wrote The letter to Umair bin Saad: As for what follows: It is from among the Muslims before you that they write to their slaves on the people’s issue."
"22643","(22643) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He disliked that A man writes to his servant if he does not have a letter."
"22644","(22644) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Burqan narrated to us, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, he said: Ibn Umar wrote to a servant of his, Then he came to him with his star when he arrived and said: Where did you get this from? He said: I was asking and doing. He said: Do you want to feed me with people’s dirt? You are free and you have this star."
"22645","(22645) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Fara`i, on the authority of Abu Laila al-Kindi, that Salman wanted to write to a boy of his, so he said: From where? He said: Ask the people. He said: Do you want to feed me with people’s dirt? He refused to write it to him."
"22646","(22646) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, he said: If he wishes, he can write to his servant, and if he wishes, he may not. He writes it."
"22647","(22647) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Hamid told me, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: He wrote to his servant and stipulated that he should not be discontented with people."
"22648","(22648) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you impose a number, then take a number, and if you impose a weight, then take a weight."
"22649","(22649) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad: He hated to advance a number and take a weight."
"22650","(22650) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Badham, he said: I saw Iyas bin Muawiyah who had drunkenness, and it was He borrows the weight of the reed and gives it back by weight. (Bukhari 1989)"
"22651","(22651) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, that they said about a man who borrowed a number of dirhams from a man. With land, it was equal to its weight, and it was equal to its weight. They disapproved of that and said: It is not equal to anything except the equivalent of its dirhams."
"22652","(22652) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hakim ibn Ruzaiq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab: Concerning a man who was He owes one man a thousand cubs of milk, and the larger ones are sold for two hundred dirhams, and the younger ones are sold for two hundred dirhams. He said: He deprived him of his rights, so He can make it lawful if He wishes."
"22653","(22653) Ruh bin Ubadah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Weight is for weight and number is for number."
"22654","(22654) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab and al-Hasan: They They saw nothing wrong with paying off the white dirhams for the black dirhams unless there was a stipulation."
"22655","(22655) Abduh narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of Ibrahim: He did not see any harm in that. Unless it is a condition or intention."
"22656","(22656) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: Concerning a man who buys a slave girl and she keeps from him. Return the price to him and ask for your maidservant. He said: And Shurayh used to say: Return it in itself."
"22657","(22657) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Dhayal, who said: I asked Muhammad about a man who sold goods for two months. Did he stipulate that if the buyer sold it before the two months, he would pay it back? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
"22658","(22658) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, who said: I sold a slave girl to a man, and she stipulated Ali: If I follow her, he said: So I followed her, so I disputed with him to Sharih, and he said: I have agreed to sell, so I have made it clear to you. On the condition."
"22659","(22659) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Shurayh: He permitted the condition. For a few ten days."
"22660","(22660) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Tawus: He did not think it was wrong to say The decrees are for his master: set aside for me and I will hasten for you."
"22661","(22661) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Tawus, he said: There is no harm in saying To write to him: Hurry for me and I will put it aside for you."
"22662","(22662) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi: Concerning a man who said to his representative: “Remove it for you and hasten to me.” His thoughts"
"22663","(22663) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: He said about a man who used to write down a dirham to his servants. Until an appointed time, then he says to him before the time comes: Hurry for me and I will spare you. He did not see any harm. He said: And I did not see anyone who hated him except Ibn Omar, he disliked that except by chance."
"22664","(22664) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin: They disliked it in the offices to say: hasten. And I will put it down for you."
"22665","(22645) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: Concerning a man who says To write to him: Hurry for me and take it easy. He said: There is no problem with it.\n Waki` said: Sufyan disliked him in office and religion."
"22666","(22646) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Bakr Al-Muzani, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: There is nothing wrong with a man taking offers from his office."
"22667","(22667) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Rabi’ told us, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to us: Let the man be taken from Writing offers."
"22668","(22668) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He hated to interrupt his correspondence. On gold or silver, and he said: No, except by accident."
"22669","(22669) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to To the people of Medina and to the people of Mecca, or one of them. He forbade them from boycotting the writings. He said: And this we do not see. He is mighty, meaning: a peacock."
"22670","(22670) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abbas, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Adhan, On the authority of Alqamah, I heard him say: For me to lend to a man twice is more beloved to me than to give him something once. (Ibn Majah 2430)"
"22671","(22671) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever gives a gift of paper, or gives him milk, or gives a waterskin, will May He free a slave. (Tirmidhi 1957. Ahmad 4/300)"
"22672","(22672) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Dalham bin Salih Al-Kindi narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdullah Al-Kindi, on the authority of Alqamah bin Qays said: Abdullah said: I am more beloved to lent money twice than to give it in charity once."
"22673","(22673) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Husayn, Or Husayn bin Qubaisa, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that he said: Whoever gives paper, or brick, or directs an alley or a road He straightened his neck."
"22674","(22674) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: A loan twice. Like giving bitterness."
"22675","(22675) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hanzali narrated to us, on the authority of Tawus, saying: Whoever gives milk to his donor will have it in full. Aleppo: Ten good deeds that were abundant or lame."
"22676","(22676) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whoever gives milk or land will have a reward."
"22677","(22677) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Sharik narrated to us, saying: Ata narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: How excellent the thirty camels are, they carry a burden on their companion, they lend their tools, and they are given abundant wealth. And you will milk it on the day it is returned to you. (Abdul Razzaq 6860. Ahmad 2/446)"
"22678","(22678) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah bin Ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Al-Zabarqan, he said: I said to Abu Hurairah. : What is the right of camels? He said: To be given abundant wealth, to be given generosity, and to be given the stallion."
"22679","(22679) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Siyah narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amri, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: To lend two hundred dirhams twice is more beloved to me than to give it in charity once."
"22680","(22680) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Three years for my reward, meaning from his bones: the freed one, the sacrificial animal, and the man who performs Hajj on behalf of the man who did not He never performed Hajj."
"22681","(22681) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: No man lent to another. A generous loan, or money, but the lender is the better of them, and if he pays it, then it is good."
"22682","(22682) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, he said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: Because I lend Two dinars is more beloved to me than to give them in charity. If you lend them to me and they are returned to me, I will give them in charity and they will be my reward."
"22683","(22683) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace in the year of the conquest, saying: God and His Messenger forbade the sale of alcohol and pigs. And idols and the dead."
"22684","(22684) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, he said: He passed by him while he was wearing the chain. Statues from scratch are being sold, and Masruq said: If I had known that he would spend, I would have struck them, but I fear that he will torture me and tempt me. By God, I don’t know which of the two men is? A man to whom his evil deeds have been made pleasing, or a man who has despaired of his hereafter, so he is enjoying this world."
"22685","(22685) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid: A man inherited idols. Of silver, pigs, and wine, he asked about them a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they all ordered him to He breaks the idols and turns them into silver, and they all forbid wine and pigs."
"22686","(22686) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Balj al-Fazari, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’i bin Rafi’ al-Ansari: His grandfather died and left his mother to be deceived, so he mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he thought about the mother’s loss, and he said: Perhaps she It cannot be found, so it seeks for itself.\n(Abu Dawud 3419. Tabarani 4408)"
"22687","(22687) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jahadi, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade making money with mothers. (Bukhari 2283 and Abu Dawud 3418)"
"22688","(22688) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Nadr, on the authority of Abu Anas, he said: I heard Uthman say: No. Force a young man to earn money and he will steal, but do not burden a female slave with anything other than the same type of work, lest she earn by her chastity, and be chaste when He has made you chaste. May God reward you with what pleases you."
"22689","(22689) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Haram bin Uthman, on the authority of Abu Atiq, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet forbade praying. May God bless him and grant him peace from the mother’s tax, unless she is in a work situation that is due. (Tabarani 8048)"
"22690","(22690) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid, on the authority of the ruling: Concerning the Syrian dinar for the dinar. Al-Kufi and Al-Shami preferred silver, saying: There is no harm in it."
"22691","(22691) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: There is no problem with him."
"22692","(22692) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I asked Ibrahim about the Levantine dinar for the dinar. Al-Kufi and his surplus silver? His thoughts"
"22693","(22693) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: He was asked about a hundred mithqals for a hundred dinars. And ten dirhams? His thoughts"
"22694","(22694) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A Levantine dinar is exchanged for a Kufan dinar and a dirham. There is no problem if a man owes you a Kufic dinar, and he gives you a Levantine dinar and buys the surplus from him for something. They will not be separated unless what is settled between them is settled."
"22695","(22695) Zaid told us, on the authority of Musa bin Muslim, who said: I asked Tawoos, “A heavy dinar for a lighter dinar and a dirham?” He said: There is no harm in it."
"22696","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said:\n (22696) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid: Concerning a man, he turns to the man. Dinars, so the qirat is preferred as gold. He said: There is no harm in taking such-and-such dirhams with it."
"22697","(22697) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who buys gold from a man. With dirhams, he weighed dinars and increased, then took silver with the surplus. He said: There is no harm in it, and Ibn Sirin disliked that. And he said: Take with him all your gold."
"22698","(22698) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham: He disliked taking half of the dinars in gold, and half of them Silver"
"22699","(22699) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, who said: Ibn Sirin used to hate al-Wazina."
"22700","(22700) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham: He was reluctant for a man to be sold. The dinar, so he took part of it as gold and part of it as silver. He said: The judge saw no harm in that."
"22701","(22701) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Muhammad, I said: I buy small dinars and say, You Innocent of her weight? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
"22702","(22702) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Musa bin Tarif, who said: Ali entered He took a house of money, so he spread it and said: By God, I will never go to evening with a dirham in it. So he called a man from Banu Asad and said: Divide it, so he divided it evenly. It was evening, and the people said: If I had made up for it. He said: If he wished, but it was permissible, so he said: We have no need for your permissibility."
"22703","(22703) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Every account He thinks of it and takes a reward for it, so he is not in vain."
"22704","(22704) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammam bin Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Yazid al-Rashk, on the authority of al-Qasim, He said: I said to Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: What do you think about Al-Qassam’s victory? He thought about it, I said: I will work on it until the sweat on my brow dries, but he did not give me permission to do it.\n His qatada said: Al-Hasan was reluctant to earn it.\n His leaders said: And Ibn Sirin said: If it is not malicious, then I do not know what it is."
"22705","(22705) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi al-Hasan, he said: It is astonishing who The one whom people entrust until he decides between them, and then takes a reward for that."
"22706","(22706) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Husayn, on the authority of al-Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman: that Omar hated The judge of the Muslims and the owner of their spoils may receive a reward."
"22707","(22707) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: There are four for which no reward is taken: the Qur’anic Qur’an. The Qur’an, the call to prayer, the decrees, and the decrees."
"22708","(22708) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: Al-Hasan was asked about earning rickets, and he said: What do you want from them? Their call, without them, I would have been defeated by you."
"22709","(22709) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad: They used to make money for themselves and they would give it to them. Their wages"
"22710","(22710) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Hassan narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He disliked the reward of a farmer."
"22711","(22711) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Medi ibn Maymun narrated to us, on the authority of Wasil the client of Abu Uyaynah, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Omar: A man asked him and said: Did you get money from sweeping these houses? He said a harsh word about it."
"22712","(22712) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: He disliked the man handing over his servant. rickets"
"22713","(22713) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Zayd, he said: Abu Abdullah Al-Shaqri narrated to us: That Ibn Umar was asked about The sweeper’s earnings? He said: Evil, evil earnings, evil eating, evil clothing."
"22714","(22714) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade avoiding and touching people. (Bukhari 2144, Muslim 3)"
"22715","(22715) Abu Asama and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Khubayb ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hafs ibn Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade keeping away from people and touching them.\n(Muslim 1152. Ibn Majah 2169)"
"22716","(22716) Waki’ told us, he said: Musa bin Ubaidah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: He forbade. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated the sale of excommunicated goods and touching them. (Nasa’i 2107)"
"22717","(22717) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Like him.\n(Muslim 1151, Tirmidhi 1310)"
"22718","(22718) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who greets another man with food. Then the time comes, and he comes to him and says: This is your food, you have eaten it, so take it. Abraham said: He will not take it until He restores his measure."
"22719","(22719) Waki’ told us, he said: Dhabi bin Amr told us, he said: I asked Salim bin Abdullah about a man who delivers to another man. Concerning food, he comes to the marketer and takes it and says: Buy from me? He said: Whoever wants to deceive himself, take it and then sell it if he wants."
"22720","(22720) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He was asked about a land grove with two land cubits and a cubit of land. With my arms, land? His thoughts"
"22721","(22721) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: I asked the arbitrator regarding fifteen garibs of land for twenty. A stranger to the land? He saw no harm in it."
"22722","(22722) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about spinning flax by weight of flax. With weight? His thoughts"
"22723","(22723) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about spinning flax with unspun flax. Weight for weight? His thoughts"
"22724","(22724) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who passed by a slave to Aasher, and he said: Are these free? Al-Hakam said: It is nothing, and Hammad said: I fear that they will be freed."
"22725","(22725) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who passed by a mamluk on a tenth floor and said: He is free. He said: He did not think he could be emancipated with this statement, and he did not see any harm in saying it."
"22726","(22726) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who passes by a slave on the street. So he says: They are free - he intends to work - he said: They will not be freed."
"22727","(22727) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan: Concerning a man who paid to another man three thousand dirhams in speculation. So he boarded the sea and broke it, so two thousand were destroyed and a thousand remained, so that thousand was drawn and gained money. How are they divided? He said: They will not divide it until there are three thousand, and then they will divide the profit after that."
"22728","(22728) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The speculator’s capital is one thousand dirhams, and they divide the profit as they stipulated."
"22729","(22729) Rawad bin Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir: He said to Al-Hakam bin Otaiba? He said: If it has been returned to its owner, inform him that he has lost some of your wealth. So he said: Go and work with what is left, for the profit is upon him. Five thousand, they divide it. If not, he tells him that the man’s capital is ten thousand, and they divide what is more."
"22730","(22730) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim: He said regarding the mudarib: Profit on As long as they agreed upon it and the deposit was on the money, if they divided the profit, the deposit was on the money, and if they did not divide it, it would be returned. Profit on capital."
"22731","(22731) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: Concerning the speculator, if he wins, then he places, then he wins, then He set, he said: The account is based on the first capital, unless it is before that a receipt of the money, or an account by receipt."
"22732","(22732) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, who said: They are on the basis of their partnership until He seeks reward."
"22733","(22733) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers: A speculator to whom speculative money was paid in half. So he gave it to someone else for half, saying: Half to the other and half to the owner of the money.\n Abu Hashim said: Half is for the other, and whatever remains is between the owner of the money and the mediator."
"22734","(22734) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim. On the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi: Concerning two partners sharing, he said: They are not counted until they get together."
"22735","(22735) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: He disliked the Murabahah sale."
"22736","(22736) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr. And on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, they said: If the animal is destroyed, there is no return to it."
"22737","(22737) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, he said: He has more right to her. He did not recover from it, or he claimed it, or one of them died."
"22738","(22738) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Jarir, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: If If the gift was consumed, or some of it was rewarded, or it was given to a relative, he does not have the right to take it back."
"22739","(22739) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who gives a garment to the tailor and says: I ordered you to wear a rag. Then the tailor says: You ordered me to wear a shirt. He said: That is what the tailor said."
"22740","(22740) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubad Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, that livestock should not be milked except with the permission of their owners, and He said: Would any of you like to be given his drink? Is there food in it, then its door is broken down and what is in it is taken out? What is in the udders of their livestock is just like what is in your livestock. No, what is in their udders is not permissible except with the permission of its family. (Muslim 1352. Ahmad 2/57)"
"22741","(22741) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: Omar said: When you pass by a camel herdsman, call out: He is a shepherd of three things. If he responds to you, then give him a drink, and if he does not respond to you, then bring them to him, sweeten them and drink them, then grate them."
"22742","(22742) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ismah, he said: I heard Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri He says: It is not permissible for a man to milk a male camel that has been mashed except with the permission of its owner. Indeed, its seal is its draining, if he is a widower Let the shepherd call out three times to the people, and if he answers, let them drink. Otherwise, let two men catch him and let them drink. (Ahmad 3/46, Bayhaqi 360)"
"22743","(22743) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: I was A young boy was herding sheep for Uqba bin Abi Mu’ait. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr came, and they had fled from The polytheists, and they said: O boy, do you have any milk to give us drink to drink? I said: I am trustworthy, I am not your legs, so the Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do you have a trunk that the stallion has not jumped on? I said: Yes, they fought, so I brought her to them, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, detained her. He wiped the udder and said goodbye, then he came to him. Abu Bakr approached a sinking rock, so he milked into it and drank, and Abu Bakr drank and I drank, then he said to the udder: Squeeze, so he reduced.\n(Abu Ali 4964 and Ibn Hibban 7061)"
"22744","(22744) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kathir, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to Medina while the people were greeting public dates. And the two and three years, and he said: Whoever advances in dates, let him advance in a specified measure and a specified weight for a specified period. (Bukhari 2240, Muslim 127)"
"22745","(22745) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If you call Qafiz and Ajala on the ladder, there is no problem."
"22746","(22746) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. And Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Aswad, is like him."
"22747","(22747) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Omar Al-Birani Yahya bin Ubaid, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas says: There is no harm in giving peace of food in a specified measure for a specified period."
"22748","(22748) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I asked him about peace in food? He said: There is no problem with it, a specified measure for a specified period."
"22749","(22749) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Razin bin Sulayman al-Ahmari, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: He said in the Salam: Do not delay it so that you can add more to him, and do not delay it so that you can lose it."
"22750","(22750) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He did not see any harm in paying in advance. A man pays for food in a specified measure and for a specified time, unless it is for crops or dates before it becomes ripe."
"22751","(22751) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Al-Mujalid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: We used to negotiate with the tribes of the Levant regarding wheat and raisins, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among us."
"22752","(22752) Ibn Abi Zaydi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir: He said, “In the salam there is ghee.” He said: Name a known measure and a known time."
"22753","(22753) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Abu Misra used to say salaam in Wheat"
"22754","(22754) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Kulayb ibn Wa’il, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: A man came to me asking me to lend him money. A dirham for food for a specified period: Every grain of wheat for a dirham and every grain of barley for a dirham. He said: Good."
"22755","(22755) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Bura, who said: Ibn Umar said: There is no harm in the greeting if it is in the A specified amount for a specified period."
"22756","(22756) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Ibn Masoud did not He sees peace in everything as a means of protection for a specified term, except for animals."
"22757","(22757) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Al-Mujalid, saying: Abu Burda and Abdullah disagreed. Ibn Shaddad in Salam, so they sent me to Ibn Abi Awfa and I asked him? He said: We used to greet wheat, barley and raisins at the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr did not. Do we know if his companions said anything about him or not?\n(Bukhari 2243. Abu Dawud 3459)"
"22758","(22758) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Hassan al-Araj, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I bear witness that the guaranteed advance is for a specified term. Indeed, God has permitted it and permitted it, then He recited: {If you contract a debt for a specified term... Named, so write it down}"
"22759","(22759) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Tha’labah ibn Al-Hakam, who said: We attacked the enemy’s sheep, so we attacked them. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the pots to be filled, and they were filled, and he said: It is not permissible to loot. (Ibn Hibban 5169 Hakim 134)"
"22760","(22760) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, he said: He forbade. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of forbidding and mutilating. (Bukhari 5516. Ahmad 4/307)"
"22761","(22761) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Jafar, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him about looting, and he said: Whoever loots is not one of us. (Ahmad 3/1401 Tahawi 49)"
"22762","(22762) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, who said: A man from the Prophet’s companions told me May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: We were with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, during a battle, and a famine struck us. We seized sheep before they were divided, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us walking, leaning on his bow until... He came to us at our place and rewarded it with his bow, and said: Depredation is not more permissible than death. (Abu Dawud 2698, Bayhaqi 61)"
"22763","(22763) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mudrik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: We do not seek a reward of honor to which Muslims raise their heads while still being believers.\n(Tayalisi 823, Abd bin Hamid 525)"
"22764","(22764) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Khalaf narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Whoever repents of his will will be robbed of his own soul. It is an honor that Muslims are known for, but he is not one of us. It was said to Abu Al-Zubair: On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 4391, Ahmad 3/395)"
"22765","(22765) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub Al-Masry told me, he said: Ayyash bin told me Abbas Al-Himyari, on the authority of Abu Al-Husayn Al-Hajri Al-Haytham, on the authority of Aamir Al-Hajri, who said: I heard Abu Rayhani, the companion of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to forbid prophethood."
"22766","(22766) Affan narrated to us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Labid, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Samra: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the practice of looting. (Ahmad 5/62, Abu Dawud 2696)"
"22767","(22767) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, on the authority of the client of Lujaynah, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Zayd bin Khalid Al-Janni, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He forbade The prophecy and the example.\n(Ahmad 5/193 Tabarani 5264)"
"22768","(22768) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan hated partners and those who speculated in goods, and he was Ibn Abi Layla says: There is no harm in it."
"22769","(22769) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: He disliked partnering with offers."
"22770","(22770) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Partnership and debt speculation should not be And the deposits, and the offers, and the absent money."
"22771","(22771) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad: He hated associating with offerings."
"22772","(22772) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Bakr, who said: A man from the people of the desert married his daughter Wasaq Her dowry, then he died, so she disputed with her brothers about her dowry to Omar ibn al-Khattab, and Omar said: As for what you found of your dowry standing? With it, it is yours, and as long as your father took possession of it, you have nothing to do with it."
"22773","(22773) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih: He imprisoned a man as a servant who sold her to his daughter.\n Ibn Idris said: I saw Ibn Abi Laila imprison a man with a servant who sold her to his daughter."
"22774","(22774) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shuraih and Abi Abdullah al-Jadali: They imprisoned a man who took part of his daughter’s dowry."
"22775","(22775) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ubaid Abi Qadamah, he said: Omar’s decree Ibn al-Khattab on women’s dowries: He who is worthy of his own right is more deserving of it."
"22776","(22776) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A child shall not be in debt to his father."
"22777","(22777) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a free man makes a bet and he acknowledges that, then he is a bettor. Until the one who pledged it redeems it, or redeems himself."
"22778","(22778) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He used to hate buying children’s gambling from The boys, and Hasan used to make a concession in it."
"22779","(22779) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Everything that involves gambling is of The facilitator"
"22780","(22780) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Harmaliya, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: There is no harm in white Boys play with it, meaning they buy it."
"22781","(22781) Hammad bin Masadhi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, who said: There is no harm in him."
"22782","(22782) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning Mamluk, he said to his master: By my name from so-and-so with such and such. And such-and-such, and you have five hundred dirhams, or a man came and took a guarantee. He said: Sell your boy from so-and-so for such-and-such, and you have five hundred dirhams. He said: He invalidates your condition."
"22783","(22783) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is not permissible, or A word like it."
"22784","(22784) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Abu Ya’qub al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Khaled ibn Abi Malik, who said: I pledged allegiance to Muhammad ibn Saad came and said: Bring your hand so that I may wipe it, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Blessing is in the one who wipes.\n(Abu Dawud 168)"
"22785","(22785) Zaid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He hated the fine cloth, mixed with it."
"22786","(22786) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, who said: Ibn Sirin disliked al-baz for speculation."
"22787","(22787) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: He used to hate it for a man to hand over his belongings to another man. Mudarib and withholding dirhams from him."
"22788","(22788) Khaled bin Abdul Rahman bin Bukair told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: A man adorns his garment. As he pleases"
"22789","(22789) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: There is no harm in adornment. He hates cheating."
"22790","(22790) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Usama bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Sa’d: They passed by Ali had a beautiful maid, so he called for her and looked at her and made her sit on his lap, and he wiped her head and prayed for her. With blessings"
"22791","(22791) Waki’ told us, he said: Osama bin Zaid told us, on the authority of some of his sheikhs, he said: Omar said: If one of you wants to do good to a slave girl, let him adorn her, and circumambulate With it, God’s provision is exposed to it."
"22792","(22792) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Ala’ ibn Abd al-Karim narrated to us, on the authority of Ammar ibn Imran, a man from Zaid Allah, on the authority of One of them, on the authority of Aisha: She saw her maid and went around with her and said: Perhaps we will hunt some young men with her. Quraysh"
"22793","(22793) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub and Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad: That a man dyed a garment that had the color of rawi. Then a man came and said: How much do you sell the drug for? He remained silent, then he bargained with him and bought it from him. When he took it, he did not have a club, so he disputed with him to Sharih and said: If only He was able to decorate his garment with something better than that, so he decorated it, so he rewarded him for it."
"22794","(22794) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Burda, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar came as a servant of his. He was selling wet clothes, and he said: Cut them, for that is better. A boy of his came to him and he was selling loose clothes, so he said: If the clothes are tight. Spread it while you are sitting, and if it is wide, spread it while standing."
"22795","(22795) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Shuraih: He used to fight back from hardship."
"22796","(22796) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, that he used to recover from hardship."
"22797","(22797) Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh: He was rejected from burying, but not from ibaq. Al-Adfan: the one who hides in Egypt, and Al-Ibaq: the one who joins his land."
"22798","(22798) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Amir, who said: It is refuted from the defects of the nail, and it is refuted. From the shameful Levant"
"22799","(22799) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Jahm al-Azdi, he said: I disputed until... A slice of a mule and a donkey."
"22800","(22800) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh: He used to refute someone who Every defect."
"22801","(22801) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Shuraih: He was not deterred from stumbling. And he says: All animals stumble.\n Waki` said: Sufyan said: It is a defect that must be removed from it."
"22802","(22802) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Shurayh: He did not turn away from stumbling blocks, and he used to say: Every animal. You stumble"
"22803","(22803) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, he said: It was concluded to Sharih in a verse. Eating flies, he said: good milk and free fodder, so he permitted it."
"22804","(22804) Muadh told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Al-Rudaini, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Omar: He was a forced labourer, and it was stipulated that he would not be addicted to being naked."
"22805","(22805) Waki’ narrated to us, Fudail bin Ghazwan narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: When he hid his land He stipulated that her owner should not expose her to her."
"22806","(22806) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar: That a man was farming He satisfied him with the virginity, so he said to him: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab: You are the one who feeds the people with what comes out of them."
"22807","(22807) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: He disliked that the earth be filled with virgin soil."
"22808","(22808) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Hassan, he said: Sakhr narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Ja’far: He hated for the earth to become muddy. Excuse me"
"22809","(22809) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Babi, the client of Umm Salamah, or Aisha, he said: I saw Saad carrying a pile of people’s virgins to a land of his own, called “Zaghaba”, so I said to him, O Abu Ishaq, Can I bear this? He said: A lump of hair is a lump of love."
"22810","(22810) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: Concerning his saying: {And he does not refuse. The witnesses, when they are called. He said: If you have the witnesses, then you have been called."
"22811","(22811) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan: When he begins to bear witness and when he is called to perform it."
"22812","(22812) Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: In his saying: {And the witnesses do not refuse when they are called} He said: This is the man who bears witness to the witness, then he supplicates for her."
"22813","(22813) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, saying: I said to Abu Majliz: I will be called to witness, and I He forced him? He said: Leave what you dislike, but when you are asked and called, then respond."
"22814","(22814) Waki’ told us, he said: Zaid bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He who is called to be a witness. So it is obligatory, but he should only bear witness to what he knows."
"22815","(22815) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Thabit narrated to us, saying: I heard Ata’ being asked: {And the father of the martyrs does not refuse when they are called} Before they witnessed it or after? He said: No, but after what they witnessed."
"22816","(22816) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: If they had They witnessed it."
"22817","(22817) Wakee’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The one who bears witness has a choice as long as he does not bear witness."
"22818","(22818) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Saeed, who said: He who has the evidence."
"22819","(22819) Shababah told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: (And the witnesses do not refuse when they are called) He said : If they had testified before this."
"22820","(22820) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: (And the witnesses do not refuse when They were called) He said: If they have witnessed."
"22821","(22821) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, who said: People used to quarrel over a covenant. Omar said: Whoever revives a land, it will be his for him."
"22822","(22822) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Thaqafi, who said: Omar wrote: He is one of the He revived a dead land, so he has more right to it."
"22823","(22823) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of Ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever revives a dead land will have a reward for it, and whatever it consumes is good for him. He spoke the truth\n(Ahmad 3/313, Ibn Hibban 5203)"
"22824","(22824) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who He revived a dead land and it belongs to him, not to an unjust race. (Abu Dawud 3071, Malik 26)"
"22825","(22825) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, and he narrates it, saying: Whoever revives a land is subject to a claim. From Egypt, he has a reward until he finds it."
"22826","(22826) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Whoever revives any of the dead on earth, it will be for him. I looked at her"
"22827","(22827) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: like the hadith of Umrah."
"22828","(22828) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever revives a dead land will be the owner of it."
"22829","(22829) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whoever revives a dead land that had not belonged to anyone before him What a blessing\n Hisham said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote about that."
"22830","(22830) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Hamid Al-Himyari, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever leaves an animal with its property, it belongs to the one who brought it to life. (Abu Dawud 3519. Darqutni 68)"
"22831","(22831) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about a man who left his animal in the barren land. Then a man took it, repaired it, and took care of it until he repaired it? He said: This is for the one who revived it."
"22832","(22832) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever surrounds a wall around a piece of land, it belongs to him. (Abu Dawud 3072. Ahmad 5/12)"
"22833","(22833) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of the ruling: Concerning a man who gave a gift to a man who was in debt. He said: He has no right to return to it."
"22834","(22834) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Shu`bai, he said: Al-Hakam said to me: Ibn Abi Layla came to me and asked me. On the authority of a man who owed a man a debt and he paid it back to him. Does he have to take it back? I said: No. I asked Hammad and he said: Yes, he may return it."
"22835","(22835) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, he said: A woman died belonging to a maternal uncle. He was well-off, so she left behind a servant and a young son. Sa`id bin Jubayr said: There is no harm in the father apportioning his children’s shares from the servant. And he entered upon her."
"22836","(22836) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Sufyan bin Al-Ala’ told us, he said: I asked Al-Hasan and Tawus about that, and they said: There is no problem. To have intercourse with her."
"22837","(22837) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Musa bin Sa’id: That his grandmother died with Abu Burda, so Abu Burda supported some of Her neighbours, I said: Ibn Aoun narrated to you, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: If a man wants to take away his children’s maidservants while they are young, he should straighten them out. He paid a price and testified to them about its price. He said: Yes, I heard it."
"22838","(22838) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abd al-Malik: That a woman died and left behind a young son and a female servant. So the father wanted to buy the slave girl, and Sa`id said: Value her in the market, then vouch for her price. Then do with it whatever you want."
"22839","(22839) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of his father, saying: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote that A wage is taken from the people of the market."
"22840","(22840) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Abi Al-Haytham Al-Attar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Asbagh bin Nabata, he said: We were In the time of Ali, whoever races to a place in the market has more right to it than the night."
"22841","(22841) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Tamim al-Rusabi narrated to us, saying: I asked Al-Hasan about the market shops? He thought about selling it, buying it, and renting it."
"22842","(22842) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of a man from the people of Medina, who said: He entered Omar bin Al-Khattab was riding in the market, and he saw a shop that had been built in the market, so he broke it."
"22843","(22843) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Mujalid bin Saeed, who said: The first person to take wages from the market Increase"
"22844","(22844) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Wabar bin Abi Dalila al-Taifi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Maimun bin Masika, Waki` said: And he praised him well, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: May the debt and punishment of the one who is present be freed. (Abu Dawud 3423, Ibn Hibban 5089)"
"22845","(22845) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dhakwan Abi Al-Zanad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Rumuz Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The withdrawal of the rich is unjust, and who It has been referred to a commander, so let him occupy it. (Bukhari 2287, Tirmidhi 1308)"
"22846","(22846) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Marwan Abi Uthman Al-Ijli, saying: Abdullah bin Masoud: If Al-Ma'ak were a man, he would be a bad man, and Al-Ma'ak is a party of injustice."
"22847","(22847) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Shuraih: Al-Ma’ak is a part of injustice."
"22848","(22848) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Al-Mattal Injustice"
"22849","(22849) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Ma’ak is a part of injustice."
"22850","(22850) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Awdi: that Daniel was the first to differentiate between Witnesses"
"22851","(22851) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mahrez bin Salih: that Ali separated between the witnesses."
"22852","(22852) Omar bin Ali bin Ata bin Muqaddam told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, who said: I heard the ruling saying: It begins. With the shroud, then the debt, then the will."
"22853","(22853) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Abraham, who said: He begins with the shroud, Then the debt, then the will, then the inheritance."
"22854","(22854) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Abraham, who said: He begins with the shroud before the religion."
"22855","(22855) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir and Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, the same."
"22856","(22856) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It begins with the shroud before the religion."
"22857","(22857) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: It begins With the shroud, then the debt, then the will."
"22858","(22858) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, who said: We used to give the people of the sheep in exchange for That they give us such-and-such of cheese, such-and-such of ghee, such-and-such of whey, so I asked my scholars. And Masrooq and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila? All of them forbade me from it."
"22859","(22859) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed: That a man asked his servants, and more than one of them. The companions of Abdullah Anhu? They thought about it."
"22860","(22860) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: Two sales cannot be separated except by mutual consent. (Bayhaqi 271)"
"22861","(22861) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ghiyath, on the authority of Abu Zur’i: He sold a horse and gave its owner a choice after that. The sale. Then, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: The sale is by mutual consent. (Abu Dawud 3452. Tirmidhi 1248)"
"22862","(22862) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The option was not made except after the sale. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to a Bedouin man, and he gave him a choice after the sale. (Ibn Majah 2184, Bayhaqi 270)"
"22863","(22863) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Tawus: He used to swear that he had no choice except after being satisfied."
"22864","(22864) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Qasim al-Ja’fi narrated to us, on the authority of his father, that Maimun bin Mihran said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The sale is by mutual consent, and the option is after the deal. It is not permissible for a Muslim to deceive another Muslim.\n(Abdul Razzaq 14264)"
"22865","(22865) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad: Al-Hasan ibn Ali bought from his wife her share of His inheritance, then he said: If I die, then give me a choice."
"22866","(22866) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh: Concerning a man who rented a house for months, or He said for a while, so he remained calm, then he wanted to leave it, so he said: If he brings the keys, then he is innocent, and he will have a reward. He settled down"
"22867","(22867) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, similar to the hadith of Abbad."
"22868","(22868) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: He will be rewarded as long as he lives."
"22869","(22869) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Salam, he said: I asked Muhammad bin Sirin about a man who sold goods for two months. And he stipulated that if he sold it before the two months, he would pay it in cash? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
"22870","(22870) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who buys a house, and the buyer says to the seller: When You brought its price and he responded to you, saying: His condition is invalid and the sale is permissible."
"22871","(22871) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Every condition in a sale, the sale is void."
"22872","(22872) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: There are only three things that cultivate: a man who has been granted land, and he cultivates what he was given, and a man who has land, and he cultivates it. And a man who acquired land for gold or silver. (Abu Dawud 3393; Ibn Majah 2449)"
"22873","(22873) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Abi Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Hanzali bin Qays, who said: I asked Rafi’ bin Khadij about renting white land for gold and silver? He said: Permissible, there is no problem with it."
"22874","(22874) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdullah, he said: I asked Sa’d about Renting land for gold and silver? He said: There is no problem with it, that is a loan of land."
"22875","(22875) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, he said: There is no problem. For renting land with gold and silver."
"22876","(22876) Yahya bin Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: There is no harm in renting land. White with gold and silver."
"22877","(22877) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah ibn Umar, who said: There were Salim, Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, and Urwah. And Al-Zuhari do not see any harm in renting white earth with gold and silver."
"22878","(22878) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: An example of what you do is to rent the white land for gold and silver."
"22879","(22879) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abul-Fadl, on the authority of Salem, who said: As for the white earth, We deny her with gold and paper."
"22880","(22880) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in a man renting white land for gold. And the paper, and he did not want to rent it for it."
"22881","(22881) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Dinar, who said: I asked Abu Ja’far about the white land. Are there trees or crops in it? Should we rent them for dirhams and dinars? He said: It is good. This is what we do to Medina."
"22882","(22882) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ikrimah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Labiba, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Sa`d, who said: We used to cover the land at the time of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him because of the crops on the brooks, and what pleased him with water from them. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade us. About that, he commanded us to decorate it with gold and paper. (Abu Dawud 3384, Ahmad 1/178)"
"22883","(22883) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab about an orphan of mine. Does he have a land? He said: If it is expensive, decorate it with gold and silver."
"22884","(22884) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Ishaq, he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about leasing the land? He said: There is no harm in it."
"22885","(22885) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, who narrated it, saying: Whoever plants in the land A people without their permission, so he does not get any of the crops, and his expenses will be returned to him. (Abu Dawud 3396. Tirmidhi 1366)"
"22886","(22886) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, who said: The Prophet passed by, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace over a crop that was shaking, so he asked about it, and they said: A man who cultivated land without the permission of its owner, so he ordered him to He returns it and takes her maintenance. (Abu Dawud 3392. Tabarani 4267)"
"22887","(22887) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far al-Khutami, who said: My uncle sent me and a boy of his to Sa’id. Ibn Al-Musayyab said: What do you say about the farms? He said: Ibn Umar did not see anything wrong with it until he narrated a hadith about it on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, came to Banu Harithah and saw crops in the land of Dhahir, and said: How good is the planting of Dhahir. They said: It is Not by Zahir. He said: Isn’t the land the land of Zahir? They said: Yes, but he farmed so-and-so. He said: Return your expenses to him and take your crops. Rafi’ said: We returned your expenses to him. And we took our crops. Sa`id said: Make your brother poorer, or force him to bear a burden."
"22888","(22888) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: It is not permissible for a Jew to bear witness. And the Christian except when traveling, and it is not permissible except upon a will."
"22889","(22889) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: That a man from Khath’am died in Daquqa and he did not receive the witness. He did not follow his will except two Christians. Abu Musa swore to them after the afternoon prayer that he had not betrayed them, nor concealed them, nor changed them. Indeed, it is your will, so he approved your testimony."
"22890","(22890) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaydah: {or two others besides you} He said: From the People of the Book."
"22891","(22891) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, {or two others from other than you} He said: from other than your family. Your religion"
"22892","(22892) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: He said something like that."
"22893","(22893) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Al-Taymimi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Majlis: He said something like that."
"22894","(22894) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah informed us, on the authority of someone who heard Saeed bin Jubayr say something like that."
"22895","(22895) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mansour and more than one person narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: From other than your clans."
"22896","(22896) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Did you ask Ubaydah about that? He said: From other than the people of your religion."
"22897","(22897) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam Ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin {or two others besides you} He said: from all Boredom"
"22898","(22898) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman Al-Jumahi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: Concerning the Almighty’s saying: {or Two others from among you} He said: They are among the people of inheritance."
"22899","(22899) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Whoever denies that he A guarantor is not a guarantor."
"22900","(22900) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’, or a person said to him: The man is arrogant. With guarantee? He said: No."
"22901","(22901) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father: He did not see rent. And the guarantee."
"22902","(22902) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, he said: I asked him about the clay that... How to dye clothes two by one? His thoughts"
"22903","(22903) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who surrendered to another man over fresh food, but he did not He met him until the hadith of that year became obsolete. He said to him: The hadith of the year in which he met him, and he was gentle. He says that"
"22904","(22904) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: He gives him the hadith of his Sunnah which He will be sued for it."
"22905","(22905) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Shurayh and Abdullah: They used to say about a man He built in a people’s yard without their permission: he has the right to cancel it, but if he built with their permission, he has the right to pay."
"22906","(22906) Hafs narrated to us, or I narrated on his authority, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ali bin Ubaid Allah Al-Ghatfani, on the authority of Ali In the same way"
"22907","(22907) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Who built in The right of a people without their permission has the right to renounce it, and whoever denies the right of a people without their permission has the right to rescind it."
"22908","(22908) Waki’ told us, he said: Zakaria told us, he said: I asked Amir about a man who lent his neighbor a wall and he built on it. So he wanted to remove its building, so he said: The owner of the wall will be fined for what he spent."
"22909","(22909) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Abi Kulayb, on the authority of Ibrahim: A man lent another man a loan. He built a wall on it, and he wanted to remove its builder, so Shurayh said to the owner of the wall: Place your foot wherever you want, meaning Its builders will be uprooted."
"22910","(22910) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of his leaders and Abu Hashim, who said: Whoever gives permission to a man to build and then He wanted to take it out, so he got the price of the builder."
"22911","(22911) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’tha’i: A man lent a man a wall and he built it. Ali, so Shurayh said to the owner of the wall: Repay him your expenses."
"22912","(22912) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh: He used to say: If they disagreed about criticism You have the good, the beautiful, and the good. If you go with the upper, leave the lower."
"22913","(22913) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Jarrah, he said: Musa bin Salem told me, he said: When Al-Hajjaj evacuated his family The land: A woman came to me with a letter claiming that the one who freed her father: This is what Talha bin Ubaidullah bought from So-and-so bin So-and-so bought from his girl a dinar or a dirham for five hundred dirhams, with the good, the good, and the beautiful."
"22914","(22914) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abbas, on the authority of his father, he said: He bought Two men brought a camel out of the marrow, and he stipulated that they should be satisfied with the money, so he brought them to his place and brought out for them a sack, so they spoiled it. Then he took out a bag for them and they showered on it, and Hudhayfy said: By God, I am one of you. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever stipulates a condition from his companion and does not fulfill it, is like one who gives away his neighbor without his prohibition.\n(Ahmad 5/404)"
"22915","(22915) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man gives food to a boatman, he is responsible for what is lacking."
"22916","(22916) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ata’: Concerning a man who rented food to the land of Bakil, If it increases, then it is up to them, and if it decreases, then it is up to them. He said: If the people are satisfied with that and acknowledge it, then there is no problem."
"22917","(22917) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: Concerning a man who hires a boatman on the condition that The decrease is upon him, and the increase is for him. He said: The increase is for the owner of the food, and the decrease is for the boatman."
"22918","(22918) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, who said: I heard al-Hasan and he was asked about the mariner carrying Food? He said: The increase is his and the decrease is his."
"22919","(22919) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh, on the authority of Abu Ayyad, on the authority of Uthman: He saw no harm in selling everything before he received anything except the measure and weight."
"22920","(22920) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, similar to him."
"22921","(22921) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, the same."
"22922","(22922) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: If a man buys something that cannot be measured or weighed, then he should not It is unfortunate that he sells it before he takes possession of it."
"22923","(22923) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibrahim: Concerning a man who makes a sale before he He takes it, he said: He only says that about measure and weight."
"22924","(22924) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The prohibition was only In what is measured and weighed, I do not consider anything other than that to be the best."
"22925","(22925) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, similar to him."
"22926","(22926) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Shu`bi narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hakam and Hammad, saying: Everything that cannot be measured or weighed, so let it not be It is unfortunate that he sells it before he takes possession of it."
"22927","(22927) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: I said to Al-Qasim bin Muhammad: A man buys goods while he is absent. Should I sell it before it arrives? Al-Qasim said: We used to say: until he comes forward."
"22928","(22928) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he heard Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan say: I heard Omar say: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Gold for silver is usury, except a hay and a hay, and silver for silver is usury, except a hay and a hay. And barley for barley is usury, except for a ha and a ha, and dates for a date is usury, except for a ha and a ha. (Bukhari 2134, Muslim 1210)"
"22929","(22929) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalababi, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath, he said: We were in a battle. And Mu'awiyah was upon us, so we acquired gold and silver, so Mu'awiyah ordered a man to sell them to the people for their gifts, so the people hastened So, His servants stood up and comforted them and returned it. Then the man came to Mu’awiyah and complained to him. Then Mu’awiyah stood up as a preacher and said: What What about the men who narrate stories about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that we do not hear? Then his servants stood up and said: By God, we will narrate to us on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, even if his Mu’awiyah dislikes it. The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do not sell gold for gold, nor silver for silver, nor barley for barley, nor dates for dates. Nor salt for salt except like for like, equal for equal, an eye for an eye. (Muslim 1210, Abu Dawud 3342)"
"22930","(22930) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Ata bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Saeed, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, distributed among us a meal of different dates, some of which were better than others. Some, so we went to increase it among ourselves, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us except as a measure for a measure.\n(Bukhari 2080, Muslim 1216)"
"22931","(22931) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abu Sa’id: He heard the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: A dinar for a dinar and a dirham for a dirham. There is no surplus between them, and a short term cannot be sold for a later time. (Bukhari 2178)"
"22932","(22932) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted the like. (Nasa’i 6163)"
"22933","(22933) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: A dirham is not worth two dirhams, nor is one saa’ for two saa’s. A dinar is for a dinar and a dirham. In dirhams. (Bukhari 2080, Muslim 1216)"
"22934","(22934) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Ghazwan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Silver for silver, weight for weight, like for like, and gold for gold, weight. By weight, like for like, so whatever exceeds it is usury, and its fruit cannot be sold until it appears to be good. (Ahmad 2/262)"
"22935","(22935) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Fudail bin Ghazwan, he said: Abu Dihqani narrated to me, he said: I was sitting at Abdullah bin Omar, and he said: A guest came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to Bilal: Bring us food, so Bilal went to Two Saa's of dates, so he bought for her a Saa' of good dates, and their dates were smaller, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, liked the dates. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Where are these dates from? So he told him that he had exchanged two sa's for one sa', and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Give us back our dates. (Ahmad 2/21, Abu Ali 5710)"
"22936","(22936) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Abu Diqaqani, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Like him"
"22937","(22937) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Ubad ibn Al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, and barley for barley. And salt for salt, like for like, hand to hand. If these types differ, then sell as you wish if it is hand to hand. With your hand"
"22938","(22938) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, He said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Gold for gold, reward for reward, and silver for silver. Sufficient for sufficient, until salt was allocated, and His servants said: By God, I do not care if I do not live in a land in which there are enemies.\n(Nasa’i 6159. Ahmad 5/319)"
"22939","(22939) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Muslim Al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Mutawakkil Al-Naji narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Saeed Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, and righteousness. With wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, and salt for salt, hand for hand, like for like, so whoever adds or increases has Arbi, the taker and the giver are the same in it. (Muslim 1211. Ahmad 3/49)"
"22940","(22940) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Jabalah bin Suhaim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Omar, he said: O people, do not buy a dinar for two dinars, or a dirham for two dirhams, for I fear archers for you. It was said: What are archers? He said: It is the one you call usury."
"22941","(22941) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abbas Al-Amiri, on the authority of Muslim bin Nazir Al-Saadi, he said: He was asked Ali about a dirham for two dirhams? He said: usury."
"22942","(22942) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of fourteen of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon them, they said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, and fear virtue. Among them are Abu Bakr, Omar, Othman and Ali. And Saad, Talha and Al-Zubayr."
"22943","(22943) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, who said: A man asked Ibn Umar about gold and silver, and Ibn Umar said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, weight for weight."
"22944","(22944) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, he said: Omar said: Do not sell a dirham for two dirhams, for that is usury."
"22945","(22945) Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Early on, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from selling gold for gold and silver. For silver except equal for equal, and He commanded us to sell gold for silver and silver for gold as we wish."
"22946","(22946) Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Kalbi, on the authority of Salama bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Bakr, he said: I heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Gold for gold, weight for weight, and silver for silver, weight for weight, the excess. And the one who increases in the Fire. (Bazzar 45)"
"22947","(22947) Affan told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, he said: Habib bin Abi Thabit told us, he said: I heard Aba al-Manhal, He said: I asked Al-Bara’ bin Azib and Zaid bin Arqam about morphology? They both say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling paper for gold as a debt. (Bukhari 2180, Muslim 86)"
"22948","(22948) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Nasr bin Ali al-Jadhami narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Rabah al-Haddani, on the authority of Malaki His son Hani, she said: Aisha came to me wearing two silver bracelets, and I said: O Mother of the Believers, I will sell her to her. Badrham? She said: No, silver for silver, weight for weight, like for like."
"22949","(22949) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard Abdul Aziz bin Hakim say: I witnessed Ibn Umar and a man came to him. From the people of Basra, he said: I came from a people who spend their small dirhams and take them with them for large ones. He said: Are they increasing? He said: Yes. He said: No, except weight for weight."
"22950","(22950) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I used to sell gold With silver, and silver with gold, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him? He said: If you pledge allegiance to your companion, do not separate from him while there is confusion between you and him. (Tirmidhi 1242 and Abu Dawud 3347)"
"22951","(22951) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Hakim, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: If you spend a dinar Do not stay until you have received its price."
"22952","(22952) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: Amr heard Ibn Omar saying: Omar said: A camel of Aleppo is waiting for you, so do not look at him. It means in morphology."
"22953","(22953) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi: that Talhah spent dinars on a piece of paper, but Umar forbade him to He will separate from him until he is fulfilled."
"22954","(22954) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazeed, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Asama, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Usury is only for women. (Bukhari 2179. Muslim 154)"
"22955","(22955) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, who said: If you sell gold for silver, do not part with it. And between you and him there is a condition except “Ha” and “Ha.”"
"22956","(22956) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Uqba Abi Al-Akhdar, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about gold. It is sold for half an hour, so he said: I heard Omar ibn Al-Khattab on this pulpit and he was asked about it, and he said: Every hour of his being asked for it, so he is usury"
"22957","(22957) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They will not separate unless what is settled between them is settled."
"22958","(22958) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shuraih, he said: What is most beloved to me in terms of exchange is that they exchange each other and not have any confusion between them."
"22959","(22959) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Habib bin Shahid, who said: Badil Al-Uqaili came to Ibn Sirin and a man with him, and he said: This man is asking you about morphology, and he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it, and Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman."
"22960","(22960) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab: That Ali and Uthman forbade Conjugation"
"22961","(22961) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sulaym bin Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, on the authority of Abu Imamah, he said: I heard it. He says: Exchange is usury."
"22962","(22962) Waki’ told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ya’qub, on the authority of Yahya al-Tawil, he said: Ali was asked about morphology? He said: That is usury."
"22963","(22963) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Khalda narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliya, he said: If I passed by the house of a money changer and I He is thirsty and I have not given him water to drink."
"22964","(22964) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: Whoever sells a palm tree after it has been planted, its fruit is for the seller unless the buyer stipulates it, and whoever sells a slave and has money The seller has nothing to do with it unless the buyer stipulates it. (Muslim 80. Abu Dawud 3425)"
"22965","(22965) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kahil, on the authority of someone who heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever sells a slave and has money, his money belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates.\n(Abu Dawud 3427, Bayhaqi 326)"
"22966","(22966) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ata’ and Ibn Abi Maliki, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever sells a slave and has money, his money belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates that he says: I bought it. From you and your property, and whoever sells a palm tree that has been ripened, its fruit is for the seller unless the buyer stipulates it. (Nasa’i 4984, Abd al-Razzaq 14424)"
"22967","(22967) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir. On the authority of Ash'ath, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn Umar, they said: Whoever sells a palm tree, the fruit is for the seller unless the buyer stipulates, and whoever sells If a slave has money, the money belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it. (Nasa’i 4983, Ibn Hibban 4924)"
"22968","(22968) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, he said, Ali said: Whoever sells a slave and has money, the money It is for the seller, unless the buyer stipulates, and whoever sells a palm tree that has been pollinated, meaning: it has been pollinated, and its fruit is for the seller, unless the buyer stipulates, it was decided. By the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bayhaqi 326)"
"22969","(22969) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar said: Whoever sells a slave And he has money, so his money is his master’s, unless the one who bought it stipulates that (Muslim 1172, Bayhaqi 298)"
"22970","(22970) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utbah and Shurayh, who said: So He sold it while he had money, so his money goes to the buyer."
"22971","(22971) Waki` told us, on the authority of his people, he said: I asked the ruling about him? He said: The money is for the buyer."
"22972","(22972) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Tawus, who was asked about a man who bought a slave and stipulated his money. He said: His money is his. And if he does not stipulate, then his property belongs to his master."
"22973","(22973) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a seller is sold and he has money, his money goes to the buyer."
"22974","(22974) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he sells it and has money, then his money goes to the buyer."
"22975","(22975) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad: He saw no harm if a man sold his servant and had money. To say: I sell you and your property."
"22976","(22976) Ismail Ibn Aliyya narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad: He did not see any harm moving with any animal. And dirhams, the beast is majila and the dirhams are nasee’."
"22977","(22977) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad: In cows for cows, between them were dirhams, dirhams. NS\n Muhammad said: There is no harm in it, and he disliked it."
"22978","(22978) Some of the sheikhs told us, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no problem. To sell a camel for a camel for ten dirhams, if the animal is in advance and the dirhams are delayed, and he hates it. If the dirhams are early and the livestock is recent."
"22979","(22979) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: I heard him say: Grapes are not sold until... It prevails."
"22980","(22980) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas: That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He forbade selling grapes until they turn black. (Tirmidhi 1228 and Abu Dawud 3364)"
"22981","(22981) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Shaybah, on the authority of Isa bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Shuraih: He said in Shafi’i: according to the proportion of the prophets."
"22982","(22982) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer. On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, they said: Al-Shafi’i is based on quotas."
"22983","(22983) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amer, he said: Al-Shafi’i is on the heads of men."
"22984","(22984) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Al-Shafi’i is on the heads of men.\n Al-Hasan said: It is according to the proportion of the prophets."
"22985","(22985) Waki’ told us, he said: I heard Sufyan say: Al-Shafi’i, Al-Qasamiya, and Al-Aql are upon the heads of men."
"22986","(22986) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Abu Shayba, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: It is upon the heads of men."
"22987","(22987) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Al-Shafi’i is according to the proportion of the ansabi."
"22988","(22988) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: Al-Shafi’i is based on the punishments, and there is no pre-emption. With the doors."
"22989","(22989) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Al-Shafi’i With the doors.\n(Abdul Razzaq 14400)"
"22990","(22990) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Al-Shafi’i is for Al-Haytan."
"22991","(22991) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Al-Shafi’i regarding doors is nothing, but rather Pre-emption of punishments."
"22992","(22992) Shababā told us, on the authority of Shu`bā, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about scratching with iron, we forgot, so he thought. That is Hammad, and the ruling did not see any harm in him."
"22993","(22993) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: A representative wanted to give his master money. All of it, and he said: I will not take it for anything but stars. So Uthman wrote to him that he would free him, and he took the money and said: I will give you stars. When he saw That man took the money."
"22994","(22994) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Abu Layla, on the authority of Abu Dhabi, who said: A representative who brought money was presented to Omar. He carried it, and his master said: I will not accept it from you. I have only written to you to take from you the stars of the years for my maintenance, and perhaps you will agree with that. You die and I inherit from you. So Umar ordered the money and put it in the treasury, then he rewarded it with stars and granted him his freedom."
"22995","(22995) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm: A man wrote to a servant of his, and he stared them at him, and brought him all of them, but he refused to accept them. The master, except for the stars, so the messenger came to Omar and sent for his master. He came and offered him money, but he refused to take it, so Omar said : O Yarfa, pay it into the treasury, and he said to the master: Take it as stars, and he said to the offices: Go wherever you wish."
"22996","(22996) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no problem with a penny in exchange for two philistines hand in hand."
"22997","(22997) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, the same."
"22998","(22998) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad, who said: There is no problem with a penny in exchange for two philistines hand to hand."
"22999","(22999) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utbah and Shurayh: Concerning a man who sells a slave while he owes a debt. He said: His debt. On his master, it does not exceed its price, and if he sells it and has money, then his money belongs to the one who bought it, meaning the buyer."
"23000","(23000) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a slave is sold while he is in debt and has wealth, then his wealth belongs to the one who He bought it, and the debt is on the one who sold it."
"23001","(23001) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Ibn Aoun, Hisham, and Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Shurayh in A slave is sold and owes a debt. He said: His debt is on the one who sold him and took his price."
"23002","(23002) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: that Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhayni was brought in the name of a servant. A debtor rode him and said: He has nothing to do with his religion."
"23003","(23003) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: A man bought a mount from another man and he traveled. Ali, and when he returned, he found a defect in her, so he disputed with her to Shurayh and said: You gave him permission in her back."
"23004","(23004) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ghaylan, on the authority of Al-Hikam: Concerning a man who bought an animal and let it down, then found With a defect, he said: He restores it, and with it he restores what is between frail and fat."
"23005","(23005) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn: Two men testified at Shurayh. So the ruling was fulfilled, then one of them returned, but Sharih did not accept his return."
"23006","(23006) Waki’ and Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: Al-Hakam cannot be returned, and Hammad said: It will be returned."
"23007","(23007) Sahil bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan: About two men who gave testimony, then they all returned. So he ruled on it and said: The ruling will be rejected."
"23008","(23008) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn: That a man testified with Shurayh with a witness, and he came He came back, and Shurayh said: We have accepted your testimony."
"23009","(23009) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: If the ruling is passed, the testimony is permissible, and the witness will be fined if he returns."
"23010","(23010) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Wasil bin Abi Jamil, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Four people participated. A share in the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in crops, and one of them said: Before me is the land, and the other said: Before me is the acre. The other said: The seed has come before me, and the other said: I must work. When the seed was harvested, they went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he assigned the crops to the owner of the seed, abolished the owner of the land, granted the owner of the acre a known thing, and assigned to the owner of the work a dirham each. One day, Wasil said: I spoke about it to an alcoholic man, and he said: This hadith is more beloved to me than that of Waseef.\n Waki` said: More beloved to us than crops is trade in gold, silver, and food. This is the saying of Sufyan.\n Waki` said: We hope that half, a third, and a quarter will be permissible, because people work with them."
"23011","(23011) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: The sale by option means selling them as long as they do not separate, unless their sale is by option. (Muslim 461, Ibn Hibban 4913)"
"23012","(23012) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Salih Abi Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The two parties are at option as long as they do not separate.\n(Ahmad 3/402, Ibn Hibban 4904)"
"23013","(23013) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Jamil bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Wadhi, On the authority of Abu Barzah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The sale is for option unless they separate.\n(Abu Dawud 3451, Ibn Majah 2182)"
"23014","(23014) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Ayoub bin Utba narrated to us, saying: Abu Kathir Al-Suhaimi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The sale is for option unless they part ways after they sold it, or There will be a choice between them. (Ibn Hazm 1417)"
"23015","(23015) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki and Ata’, They said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The sale is for the option until they part with their consent."
"23016","(23016) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The sale is at option unless they separate."
"23017","(23017) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: The sale is the option unless They separate."
"23018","(23018) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi: Concerning a man who bought a beetroot from a man, and he wanted to return it. Before they separated, Al-Sha’bi ruled that it was obligatory for him, so Abu Al-Duha testified with him that a share had been brought to him. Likewise, he returned it to the seller, so Al-Sha’bi returned to Shurayh’s statement."
"23019","(23019) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Buying for option As long as they did not separate, then if Ibn Omar sold, he would leave to make the sale obligatory."
"23020","(23020) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: The sale is at option unless they separate."
"23021","(23021) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, who said: A trade for an option is not They did not separate."
"23022","(23022) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikiya, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The two sellers. By choice as long as they do not separate."
"23023","(23023) Ibn Abi Zaydah and Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: If he speaks It is permissible for him to sell it."
"23024","(23024) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Khaled bin Muhammad, on the authority of a sheikh from Banu Kinanah, who said: I heard Omar say: Selling is only by bargain or option."
"23025","(23025) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The sale is permissible even if it is not They separate."
"23026","(23026) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: Concerning a man who said to another man: If I sell you my slave, then he will be free, and the other said: If you buy it, he is free. He said: He will be freed from the seller’s money because he broke an oath before him."
"23027","(23027) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawwi, who said: Hammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He He is freed from the seller’s money because he broke the first oath."
"23028","(23028) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, who said: The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 3393 and Ibn Majah 2267)"
"23029","(23029) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and his family and companions. (Muslim 82. Abu Dawud 3398)"
"23030","(23030) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, on the authority of Saul bin Abi Hathamiya: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling the fruit for dates, and permitted it to be sold to a naked woman. With its sweetness, its people eat it fresh.\n(Bukhari 2191, Muslim 1870)"
"23031","(23031) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, forbade places of worship and graveyards. (Bukhari 2187. Ahmad 1/224)"
"23032","(23032) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, he said: Bashir bin Yasar, the client of Banu Harithah, narrated to me. Rafi’ ibn Khadij and Sahl ibn Abi Hathama narrated that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of fruit dumps. With dates, except for those who are naked, for He has given them permission. (Bukhari 2384, Muslim 1170)"
"23033","(23033) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God prohibited God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the fields and the clearings, for the clearings are for crops, and the clearings are for palm trees.\n(Bukhari 2176, Muslim 1179)"
"23034","(23034) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Salamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the places of worship and the graveyards. (Muslim 1179. Tirmidhi 1224)"
"23035","(23035) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade He greeted the sale of fruit for dates. (Muslim 1167. Ahmad 2/8)"
"23036","(23036) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ismail Al-Shaybani, who said: I sold what is in the tops of palm trees, if there is more, let them. If it decreases, then it is up to them. So I asked Ibn Umar? He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade that, because he had permitted the practice of nakedness. (Ahmad 2/11 Hakim 365)"
"23037","(23037) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and his family and companions."
"23038","(23038) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: The fields of crops are like the clearings of palm trees."
"23039","(23039) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Zayd bin Thabit narrated to me: The Messenger of God forbade the places of worship and the graveyards. (Tirmidhi 1300, Ahmad 5/185)"
"23040","(23040) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Hakim, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Dates for dates are on the heads of Palm trees are measured. He said: If there is a dinar or ten dirhams between them, there is no problem."
"23041","(23041) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Othman bin Hakim narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in selling Dates on the tops of palm trees. Dates are a measure if they contain ten dirhams or dinars."
"23042","(23042) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Umari told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Malik 23)"
"23043","(23043) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: We heard the interpretation of the Muzabanī: buying what is on the tops of palm trees for dates, and the farms: Purchasing what is in ears of wheat, barley, and barley: a man who has a palm tree inherits it or buys it in The Garden of Men"
"23044","(23044) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Mujma’, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: He said about wheat for dates as a form of interest: usury."
"23045","(23045) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir: He hated it for the length of an atom’s length. With a mudd of wheat."
"23046","(23046) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: Omar bought a horse from a man, and asked him to do so. He was pleased with him, otherwise there is no sale between them, so Omar brought a man from his own to him, and the horse became spoiled, so they made a dispute between them. So Shurayh said to Omar: Deliver what you bought, or return what you took. So he said to him: I have decided according to the truth.\n Zakaria said: Amir said: He sent him to judge Kufa, and he sent Ka’b bin Sur to judge Basra."
